/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026.mem:22:F6 moves the browser's Repo and daemon kernel into its shared holder, and the kernel's sealed writes asked where the key lives. Four ratcheted research rounds (2026-10-19) answered, each a Luna-6 YIN and YANG pair in two traded waves, YIN with live search over vendor and spec pages, YANG over the code: round one on the fork, round two on per-face custody keys, round three on the question the operator answered Mu, round four confirming the model across every vessel type. The rulings rest at #/rulings; the eight wave-two handbacks rest verbatim at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face">>. Rows `K15`, `F6`, `B1` and `X0` of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">> carry the build.
