/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026.mem:31:# ''A face's custody rows seal under its own key.'' Each PersonaGroup holds an independent random face custody key (FCK) that only its own slot tree opens, never wrapped under a vessel key; a holder of the S key or of a sibling's unlock opens none of its rows.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026.mem:49:* ''The place signer.'' A node's private place signing seed rests clear and loads at boot, so a herm serves its floor with no face (`node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442`). Either it stands as a named floor signer protected at rest, the floor then holding no custody key rather than no key, or it moves behind a boot custody door and a herm's unattended floor waits for a hand.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026.mem:50:* ''The node archive selector.'' Which veil row the node writes rests unproven against its writer chain; K15's step 0 proves it before bytes move.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026.mem:59:A YANG scout read the code and a YIN scout read the field, then they traded. The node's place seed rests clear as hex JSON, mode `0600`, and loads at boot with no hand; it signs the place KEL's inception, `carry-for` seals and floor pins, carriage presentations, the floor card and the floor-gate children (through a domain-registered door that never hands out the seed), and it reaches past the floor: the relay gate, the daemon's auth, internal asks, the device-key signer, `deriveDyadVeil` for every face's device veil, and `groupSecretOpenerFromSeed`. The place KEL commits no next key, so a stolen seed re-founds. SSH host keys, the Tor onion master key, WireGuard and ACME account keys load unattended under file permissions; systemd encrypted credentials with TPM2 bind release to the host and its boot state; Vault auto-unseal and Kubernetes secrets move trust to a machine identity; KERI pre-rotation alone makes a theft recoverable. Both scouts ranked a pre-rotated place KEL with a scoped online signer first, a named protected signer second, and a boot door third. The operator ruled the first, its next key riding the founding card, and ruled each face's device veil a random key of its own under that face's FCK. The four handbacks rest verbatim at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face">> #/r5-yin-wave1-yin-wave-one-internet-scout-place-signer onward.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026.mem:64:<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face">>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/e2e-offering-run-topology.mem:38:* The witness removes the matching plugin byte from B's staged cleartext CAS, inspects the local Crossroads evidence as partial, writes the exact source byte into B's CAS as an explicit custody control, then overwrites it with corrupt bytes and expects invalid. It compares the Genesis seed and non-CAS files before and after. It also runs an unknown-record refusal and temporarily swaps `process.env.LAR_ROOT` for a wrong-root check (`tests/e2e/nexus-offering-replication.test.ts`, lines 101–154). It does not exercise generic plugin-byte carriage: the byte is explicitly seeded by the test.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/edge-frontier-2026.mem:10:status    = "research; read 2026-10-20; the ruling landed at docs/stable-founding-road #/rulings (the edge frontier) and row K17 the same day"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/edge-frontier-2026.mem:22:A fifth fresh read of `K15` Wave B found that reading an empty edge board's absence as "aside" refused every healthy fleet's joins and key wraps, while reading it as "clear" lets a withheld raise pass. Claims read MEASURED (code or a cited source) or LEAD.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/evergreen-sweep-2026.mem:9:role      = "field research, two traded Luna-6 waves and a Sol-6 code reader (2026-10-18), on lifting shared shapes into their packages and yanking authored version numbers and deciding wall clocks; the six rulings the operator approved; the Sol plan verbatim, Markdown transliterated only"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/evergreen-sweep-2026.mem:22:After the long buildout the operator called a deep Aftermath and Evergreen pass over `packages/*/src` and `tools/` (2026-10-18): shapes two packages re-derive lift into the shared package that owns them (federated-mesh shapes into `@lararium/mesh`, TW5 shapes into `@lararium/tw5`), authored version numbers yield to CIDs and edges, and wall clocks that decide yield to causal events. A Luna-6 YIN and YANG pair read the code in two traded waves over pre-grepped inventories (281 clock lines, 373 version-shaped lines, 208 narrating comments, 76 names defined in two or more packages); a Sol-6 code reader then verified their findings against source, refuted ten, and wrote the plan as fourteen lanes. The plan rests verbatim from #/plan-refutations-and-corrections on, and #/rulings answers its open questions; the pair's wave-two handbacks rest at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-evergreen-sweep">>. Row `G37` carries the build; its standing witness (PR #53) holds today's count rather than a clean baseline, so the plan's lane 14 landed first.
