/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-field-collision-ii.mem:263:''VINDICATION'' (https://www.inkandswitch.com/keyhive/notebook/). Sedimentree compacts the Automerge commit graph by ''recursive content-addressed chunking'', with chunk boundaries set by ''the number of trailing zeros in a commit's hash'' so "peers with different sets of changes still agree on what should go into each chunk" — ''no wall clock, no coordination''; metadata overhead ~10% over the underlying data. This is a direct vindication of two of our rulings at once: (a) `epoch-binding-surfaces`'s test — "does the fold pick a WINNER or blank both paths?" — Sedimentree compaction ''picks nothing; it is not a fold at all'' ("a cut, not a fence"), exactly as the meme classes compaction; and (b) the clockless stance — its snapshot cadence is //implicit in the hash rule//, never a timestamp.
