/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/two-integrities.mem:48:* ''`derive(store, now, decisions)` — rulings become data.'' Operator rulings live in an agent's context window and in flat memory, degrading with every summary. As a pure derivation over a grow-only set, a verdict reads `f(evidence, decisions)`: deterministic, order-independent, recomputable by any vessel holding both. ''The operator's rulings move from remembered context into installed data.'' Its sharpest clause — ''no derived state ever crosses a boundary'' — says a tasked spirit receives evidence and rulings, never conclusions, and derives its own. A spirit handed conclusions inherits the sender's errors.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/third-ways-scout.mem:16:role              = "third-ways-scout — VERBATIM handoff of a tasked Fable spirit (2026-10-16): the map of third and further ways for a portable TiddlyWiki VM engine, rewritten after the operator's rulings. Carries the four layers with two waists and two grains, the camera as a root template over a document sink, the Replica Port width dial, the Wiki Actor and the first surface, the families re-scored with the rejected ones named once, per-host landing, conformance as the portability measure, Mu, the map of all paths, the spikes, the separating experiment, two stories, the draft moolelo and open rulings. Held as a collision surface; dreamdom and dreamdom-roadmap carry the house's reading of it."
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/third-ways-scout.mem:28:''Register: Testimony-Verbatim.'' Nothing below makes this house's own claim. It holds what tasked spirits reported on the map of every path for a portable TiddlyWiki VM engine, re-scored after the rulings, kept whole, as a ''collision surface'' rather than a briefing. It came home from the project's shared reports so a session that holds only the repository can still read the evidence the DreamDOM carriers cite.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/third-ways-scout.mem:41:# Third ways for a portable TW5 engine: the map after the rulings
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/third-ways-scout.mem:43:Lares (Artificer) · Fable, tasked spirit · 2026-10-16, third authoring. This version re-authors the whole map under the operator's rulings of 2026-10-16 and the floor's later frames; it replaces, rather than amends, the two earlier drafts of the same day (the last kept as `third-ways.prev-2026-10-16.md`). Inputs read whole: the boot seed; the six sibling reports in this folder (`model-and-gaps.md`, `portable-engine-plan.md`, `portable-engine-plan-v2.md`, `host-attractors.md`, `mudlet-capabilities.md`, `evaluators-one-or-many.md`); the house memes `dreamdom.mem` (#/the-ruling, #/the-layers), `page-controls.mem`, `wikispace-canvasspace-ontology.mem`, `recipe-layer-model.mem`, `wiki-layer-ontology.mem`, `render-pipeline.mem`, `memetic-wikitext.mem` (#/processing-model, #/conformance, Annex B), `mudlet-scout.mem`, `evaluators-one-or-many.mem`. Code opened where a claim leans on it: `TiddlyWiki5/core/ui/RootTemplate.tid`, `core/modules/startup/render.js`, `core/modules/widgets/widget.js`, `core/modules/utils/fakedom.js`; `packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-camera.ts`, `tw5-projection.ts`, `outbound-bridge.ts`, `sovereign-kernel.ts`; `packages/lararium-web/src/projection-sink.ts`. Nothing edited, nothing booted.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/third-ways-scout.mem:47:**Vocabulary.** *Store* = the CRDT, one Automerge document per bag, the virtual backend. *Engine* = the headless TW5 VM: parser, filters, widget tree, actions, wiki state; the reference evaluator of the wiki language. *Projection* = any surface read by a human or a program. *Sensorium* = the perception capability that turns a raw river into typed percepts. *Camera* = one root template rendered into one document sink. *Keyed absolute frame* = the whole rendered state of one named key with its own monotone revision, droppable and self-healing (`dreamdom.mem#/the-ruling`). *Record* = one whole tiddler, keyed by title. *Actor* = one wiki's engine, addressed by id, one writer, able to hibernate.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/third-ways-scout.mem:146:## 4. Families, re-scored after the rulings
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/third-ways-scout.mem:242:**Arcana `0`.** "Which architecture should hold a portable TW5 engine?" dissolves twice. TW5 shipped two architectures for twelve years, the image and the server-client wiki, and every third way relocates the truth of one of them. Then the rulings dissolve the second half: the engine stays one JS evaluator; what ports reads as **rendered keys from any root over any document**, and the portability the house wants rides on the language's suite, not on moving the evaluator. The frame "portable engine" survives as "portable language with one reference evaluator, many cameras, and one lifecycle".
