/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:16:role              = "persona-policy — the operator's rulings on the multi-persona identity core: a SESSION wears the face and the vessel wears none, so every act carries exactly ONE face (PRIVATE-all, PUBLIC-one); a switch runs as ONE session's act, recorded on the vessel and never on the wire; two faces live from one vessel never link on the wire · each PersonaGroup a CRYPTOGRAPHIC INDIVIDUAL (Sybil-of-one the accepted IoC cost, answered socially never in crypto) · DISTINCT recovery custodians per persona. Plus the two-layer pet-names (private map ⊥ public glamour) under Zooko — the pet-name FLEET-SYNCS among the human's own vessels and never PUBLICLY federates — under THE BINDING LAW: only a publicly announced Handle binds a PersonaGroup to a public glamour, so no other path may carry a persona's name onto a federating surface. Identity carries no universal index; the mesh refuses to build the SIN even to defend itself"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:32:The multi-persona identity core (persona-circle: a human as a private Circle of selves, each an all-hardened key at its own handle-index) ''carries three operator rulings'' that fix how a human's selves get worn over a vessel and how they recover. Each ruling ''bends toward the same law'': the mesh refuses a global identity-now, so it never builds the Single Identity Number even to defend itself. The rulings land 2026-07-20, dispatched to code at #64 stage 4; the session ruling (#/the-session) lands 2026-10-11 and names WHAT wears a face.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:46:The wall stays custody-by-TYPE: wearing a persona ''REQUIRES that this vessel HOLD its sovereign root'' — you sign only as a self whose secret you carry (persona-vault#wearPersona).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:61:| its own roots, device-minted (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lararium-identity#/vessel-key">>) | the persona root, held in the vessel's custody; it never travels | the worn face |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:63:| the device key, serving custody and local identity ONLY | its admit relation | access to the worn face's planes and to no other face's |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:64:| custody, the store lock, the holder | its ONE current public Handle | the EFFECTIVE recipe |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:68:''What the ruling states outright'': a vessel holds its roots and one store; a session contracts in as ONE persona; the vessel-wide parts (custody, the daemon island) serve every session and let none read another's planes; each session proves itself under its own face-scoped key. ''The remaining cells place objects as a model study read them against canon and code (2026-10-11)'': builders read those cells as the standing model, unbuilt, and a later ruling may move one. Two carriers state the model as a contract: what a session carries and how its vessel answers it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract">>), and the face-scoped proof subject a session presents at a gate (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:190:''What the code holds'': `lares persona guardian enrol` refuses a key this vessel holds in another face's set (`guardian-key-serves-another-face`) before the face's own key signs the typed first enrolment (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/persona-kel#/the-enrolment">>); each face's set rests in its own sealed row, and a guardian cuts a fresh key per face with `lares persona guardian offer`. ''Owed in code'': the bundle's carriage of a face's guardian set; the memory-card reader. The per-face sealed backup bundle stands built with its restore, rehearsed under scratch roots (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/what-the-code-holds">>); its memory import completes once a session signer stands. The shared-document road rests on Keyhive group membership, and nobody has walked it here. Three sites still bind a raw key where the lineage belongs — the antigen's presenter `nym`, the handle-card's `nym`, and the per-Nexus leaf an admit names, derived from the persona seed — so a recovery re-issues those until each re-sites (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/identity-classes#/the-honest-edges">>). Guardian count, request authentication, the veto and succession stand open at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/seed-and-nexus">>.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:228:''A label a human sets on one vessel and loses on the next names the compartment badly.'' So the two NAMES ride the ''@persona bag'' — the PersonaGroup's own private plane, which the self-slot ''FLEET-syncs same-operator'' and the DeterministicFederationGate never volunteers to a cross-operator. One multitude, every device of the one human, no stranger. No verb carries either name: a store verb's outcome and its receipt digest rest in the daemon's document in the clear, so the names ride the custody door instead. The act `selves.carry` names a face and which name; the vessel reads that name off its own sealed row and writes it onto that face's own plane from its main thread, `selves.clear` follows the row's own clear, and `selves.read` answers each carried face as its own plane names it. A face's name lands on its own plane and on no other face's, so one face's fleet learns nothing of another face (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>). ''A name rides only onto a plane whose rest seals'': while a plane's document rests in the clear on a vessel's disk, `selves.carry` refuses by that rest and the name stays on its sealed row (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/owed">>). ''No board shore stands reachable from either act'' — the wall runs structural, as it does for the follow-graph one plane over.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:244:The three rulings ''share one root'': the causal-islands law (#causal-islands: no global present, each island its own partial log) ''extended to IDENTITY''. There sits ''no global now for who-someone-is'' — no mesh-wide instant of "this human = these faces = one custodian". Every attempt to assert it manufactures the very global-now the substrate forbids (the same move carry-contract's immune system refuses for revocation, one plane over).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:262:<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/rulings">>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:10:role      = "the face intent plane: the channel of intent through each face's fleet of device vessels; the daemon's split into working memory, intent and per-vessel records; who answers an intent with no election and no clock; the far agent; and the rubric for what earns a place in a face's log"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:34:| The face's pins (group, signer, KEL prefix, device edge) | the face's custody and `@persona-<tag>` | identity belongs to the face; the floor reads none of them until the face's atom lights (`K15` step 2c) |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:49:* ''Entries append, never edit'', each signed by the atom of the device that writes it (a far agent's by its own key, #/the-far-agent). Kinds:
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:50:** `intent`: an invocation naming its verb, its arguments, its audience and its causal bound (#/no-clock). Its id is the content hash of issuer, verb, arguments and nonce, so every device derives it offline and a replayed copy carries the same id. An idempotent verb takes the empty nonce.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:68:# ''A claim steers effort'' on a long act: a claimant appends `claim`, then its outcome or `release`. Another device may append `takeover` naming the claim; a fenced effect accepts an act only from the current claim, and an idempotent one converges either way.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:76:* ''A claim never expires.'' It ends by its own outcome, by `release`, or by `takeover`. A device MAY suspect a claim stale by its own local elapsed time and decide to try a takeover; no clock value enters the log or settles anything.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:78:* ''The operator's release always wins'': a `release` or `cancel` signed for the face outranks any claim, by authority, never by order.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:86:!! The far agent ~ an AI that acts from afar
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:90:* The agent holds its own key and a narrow delegation from the face: a verb prefix, an argument policy and a causal bound in place of an expiry time.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:91:* It signs an `intent` and hands it to a ''relay seat'': a vessel of the face with a door off the local socket, opened per face, ring-gated and off by default. The relay verifies the chain and appends the entry carrying the AGENT's signature; it countersigns only its admission.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:138:# A far agent's intent, admitted by a relay, verifies on a device that never saw the relay; a revoked delegation refuses on read, the revocation arriving first or after; a relay that alters an argument breaks the signature.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:149:Row `I1` at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">> carries the build, red-first in this order: the plane and its entry kinds; stand-down and the verb classes; the read-side winner; claims, takeover and causal voids; the face-join summons moving off the daemon doc onto the plane (closing "two hearths of one face"); the daemon wiki's view pane; the rubric's witness; then the far agent's relay seat after its own research. The CLI's per-invocation face naming (the session model's commit 5) lands beside the summons move, since an intent names its issuing face.
