/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/syncer-back-parity.mem:33:''Register: Model-Standing.'' Every row below names the wire exchange it read — the request line the page issued and the status it got back. A row without one names itself as inference.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-evergreen-sweep.mem:21:Verbatim wave-two handbacks of the Luna-6 YIN and YANG spirits (2026-10-18); only Markdown transliterated to memetic-wikitext. YIN read isomorphisms first, YANG clocks and version numbers first; each then confirmed or refuted its twin against the code. A Sol-6 reader verified both and refuted ten claims; its plan and the operator's rulings rest at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/evergreen-sweep-2026">>, and a refutation there outranks a claim here.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-evergreen-sweep.mem:46:# ''MEASURED · confirmed-by-both — Shared byte equality should live at the mesh floor.'' Browser `sameBytes` at `packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-fleet-join.ts:78` and node `sameBytes` at `packages/lararium-node/src/fleet-join-custody.ts:43` are byte-identical length-plus-element comparisons. Mesh has three `bytesEqual` variants at `packages/lararium-mesh/src/sealed-chunk.ts:262-267`, `slip39.ts:350-355`, and `sealed-writer.ts:203-209`. Lift a `bytesEqual` primitive into `@lararium/mesh`; adapt null handling in sealed-writer. The sealed-chunk version accumulates XOR differences (constant-time intent), unlike early-exit variants, so do not flatten that semantic/security difference into one implementation without preserving its timing property. Node/browser copies have no such distinction. Depends only upward from node/browser; direction remains valid.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-evergreen-sweep.mem:180:# ''MEASURED — Isomorphism confirmation — twin-alone.'' Confirmed YIN findings 1–4 and 8–9 by opening the cited lines. `packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-vault.ts:269-275` owns platform-blind `readWornPersonaMount`; `packages/lararium-node/src/worn-mount.ts:9-18` imports it and binds the fs vault/warning sink. Already composed; no second node algorithm to lift. `packages/lararium-mesh/src/recovery-keel-core.ts:92-105` owns generic reconstruction/readmission; `packages/lararium-node/src/recovery-keel.ts:15-20,44-53` injects the Keyhive edge. Keep dependency direction mesh→no Keyhive. `packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-fleet-join.ts:78` and `packages/lararium-node/src/fleet-join-custody.ts:43` have identical byte equality (`length` plus indexed comparison), also repeated in mesh `sealed-chunk.ts:262`, `slip39.ts:350`, `sealed-writer.ts:203` per inventory. Lift only `bytesEqual` into `@lararium/mesh`; callers' custody transactions remain local. YIN also identifies strict mesh hex decoding (`crypto.ts:125`) as a candidate; Keyhive's `keyhive-provider.ts:114` strips optional `0x`, so retain normalization at the edge.
