/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:340:# ''K15.1 substrate proof:'' separate two-hive stores, registries, archives and key seats; interleave/reboot/replay and cross-read/mutate red probe. No FCK derived from process-global/shared state.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:342:# ''K15.1/.2 face contexts/identity ownership:'' face provider gets its own hive, event store, registry, archive, FCK and content seat; remove vessel identity delegation from face events. FCK never derives from VK. Preserve common VK only for floor metadata.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:343:# ''K15.3 sessions + F6 slice three (a′):'' bind each tab session to one face and its independent unlock; caused write asks the admitted asker tab. Uncaused sync/delegation targets an unlocked admitted tab for that named face or waits as `seal-awaits-session`. Common writes target a VK-unlocked session. Because current replacement opens old row, the chosen sealer must hold that row class's open key. No wall-clock lock; last tab returns browser to floor; node VK once per boot plus per-face authority.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:344:# ''K15.4 removal/content keys:'' keep FCK distinct from per-bag content keys; face removal rolls/revokes that face's group only. Carry guardian lifecycle and key rotation semantics.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:345:# ''K15.5 one-face restore/herm:'' restore only X's identity/archive/events/key memory/FCK/guardian set; herm transports ciphertext without face capability. Restore X and prove Y absent/unopenable.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:346:# ''K15.6 single migration fence:'' identity bytes + split stores + slot trees/FCK + archive/custody formats migrate together as one class change. Mixed legacy material refuses by name and follows re-found path; no silent cross-face import or “A now, B later.” F6 routing ships against this scoped format as one end state.
