/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:707:''Re-asked question — LEAD, confirmed-by-both:'' “After each face-bearing row has an independent root and each floor-readable item is public by design, what confidential cross-face data remains, and which custody boundary needs to unlock it?” This unasks “how do vessel-common acts unlock?” because the census classifies acts by their rows; the verb common to multiple faces does not itself require a common secret.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:709:''Candidate answer — LEAD, confirmed-by-both:'' Browser holds no VK. Dissolve all confidential identity/join/roster/dyad/archive/recovery records to per-face roots; leave only intentionally public opaque routing/transport at floor. Each admitted tab unlocks only that face's independent random FCK using that face's own slot tree. No FCK is wrapped by VK. If future node requirements identify a genuinely secret system-only payload that must survive before face unlock, give the node a separately named device custody root and open it once per boot; keep it out of browser and all face roots. If no such payload survives D/F, node has no common key either. A floor holds no vessel key. One Keyhive identity per PersonaGroup, none above them.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:720:* ''Node:'' if a named secret S class remains, one device custody-door authorization once per boot; a face-private act also needs that face's admission/FCK. If all rows resolve D/F, no common credential at boot.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:729:* ''K15 step 3:'' land an independently random FCK for each PersonaGroup, with only its own slot tree able to open it; keep FCK out of VK. Partition mixed carriers and enforce one identity per PersonaGroup.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:759:| Node founds VK, SK, and custody root; VK opens SK through serving tree. | ''CONFIRM.'' `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-session.ts:80-116,154-190,227-242` mints VK/SK, writes SK tree under VK and opens both on unlock. | twin-alone |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:765:| CLI and MCP do not each hold separate vessel secrets; face authority must be presented at the node gate. | ''CONFIRM as roadmap target.'' `stable-founding-road.mem:201` says CLI/MCP run proves face; `packages/lares-cli/src/sealed-act-door.ts:1-21`, `custody-door.ts:2-26`, `custody-frames.ts:135-202` implement the seat/door framing. | twin-alone |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:766:| Guest island is an established separate key store / vessel. | ''REFUTE as measured.'' `device-capabilities-2026.mem:142-143` identifies Mudlet as a probe/leaf behind a node and Unreal as guest island/camera-on-streaming-server, but `wiki-layer-ontology.mem:249` defines a Lua object-model guest, not an independent custody store. Separate guest-owned keys would make it a new vessel by LEAD; source does not prove they exist. | twin-alone |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:767:| Mobile/browser worker lifetime can hold custody across suspension. | ''REFUTE as authority claim.'' House matrix reports iOS no SharedWorker lifetime guarantee and Android support varies by version (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:137-140`). Safari's official extension guidance requires iOS nonpersistent background pages and says use storage to save/restore state ([[Apple Developer|https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safariservices/optimizing-your-web-extension-for-safari?changes=_5]], accessed 2026-10-19). Worker liveness cannot substitute for each tab/session's face admission. | confirmed-by-both |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:776:''MEASURED (twin-alone):'' Node daemon begins with an empty in-memory custody holder (`packages/lararium-node/src/main.ts:336-345,371-374`); lock clears held VK/SK (`custody-holder.ts:151-155`). Herm has no face slots. The private place signing seed nevertheless remains available from a clear-at-rest file and supports floor signing (`node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442,451-487`). This is the principal counterexample to the blanket browser-derived statement “floor only holds public data.”
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:780:''LEAD (twin-alone):'' Docker `harbor`, `civic`, and `mesh-scenarios` package the node rather than adding a vessel secret. State may persist across restart while volatile face/serving keys must not; unattended restart may restore only agreed floor behavior. A humanless container cannot type the one-per-boot custody unlock, so any private D/S service pauses. Do not inject credentials through environment, image layers, health checks, or orchestration. Sources: `stable-founding-road.mem:56,66-68`; `tools/lares-container.sh` at roadmap `:68`; `founding-runbook.mem:156`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:790://Frame, 2026-10-22: the operator has since ruled this conflict, so no reader takes it as open. `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road` #/rulings holds the answers: 2026-10-19 (//a shared act never makes a shared secret//, rows sorted D/F/S, with X0's scoped place signer) and 2026-10-20 (the place signer's fifth duty). The testimony below keeps its words.//
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:795:''MEASURED conflict:'' The agreed phrase “a floor holds no vessel key” cannot be applied literally to current node code. It stores a private *vessel signing seed* at floor and loads it without a human at boot. This is not the custody VK (the slot-tree key that wraps mixed carriers), but it is still a vessel private key and cannot truthfully be called public F. The serving key (SK) is a third key, wrapped by VK; no serving row currently exists. ''House ruling needed to close the lock:'' either (1) amend “floor holds no vessel key” to “floor holds no custody VK/FCK; a separately named floor signer S may exist,” and explicitly accept/protect the current signer-at-rest behavior; or (2) require this signer S to live behind a named boot custody mechanism, which changes Herm's no-human-before-face startup behavior and must state how public relay service stands before authorization. Until that ruling, the shared D/F/FCK/asker law locks, but “every floor is public-only” does not. TWIN's suggested “explicitly accept clear-at-rest” option still needs the operator's express choice; it is not silently inferred from the prior agreement.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:804:Rows refer to the common act census in `../PRIOR-YIN.md` (“Census of current vessel-common carriers and acts”) and `../PRIOR-YANG.md` (“Census — each currently vessel-common row act”), read 2026-10-19. In short: founding and slot trees; join offer/request/answer/land/pending; face slot changes and rotation; roster/labels/declarations; Keyhive/Veil archives; handle/circle routing; dyads/face proof/member/Nexus keys; transport configuration; recovery/bundle/restore; clear-custody. Their private face pieces are D; signed offers/public cards, charters, pins, public config and minimum deliberate route bytes are F. Mixed existing carriers must be split. Current browser one-VK tree: `packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-custody.ts:2-12,54-68,386-402`; current node classes: `packages/lararium-node/src/vault-carriers.ts:239-398`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:813:| ''Probe, e.g. Mudlet'' (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:133,142`) | Target seat owns D/F; probe holds no FCK or S. Reconnect token, if used, is a session credential, not row key. | Each node session presents authority at node; closing probe drops its session, node floor remains. | Outbound-only probe is not a LarVessel; it cannot turn node gate into local custody. | With A session only, ask node for B row; node refuses and probe cannot decrypt bytes locally. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:816:| ''Node daemon / full node'' (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:141`; `vault-carriers.ts:287-398`) | All node common private face rows D; public card/charter/floor data F; future serving rows are S only once instantiated. Current place signing seed is separate floor S exception. | Each face row session requires its face; node S custody target once per boot if approved; process lock/restart drops volatile keys. Current place seed auto-loads from file without prompt. | Current VK wraps mixed carriers. Node archive selector still unresolved in prior census. Floor signer conflict above must be ruled. | Boot with no VK: F service works; no face row opens. Unlock A and attack every B carrier/rotation/restore directly: fail unchanged. Verify place signer is separately recorded, not mislabeled F or SK. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:817:| ''Hearth composition'' (`packages/lararium-node/src/main.ts:353-374`; `vessel-caps.mem:139-143`) | Same node rows and S as node; hearth adds no new principal. | Per-face after node boot; shutdown/lock clears face and serving keys to floor. | Composition today follows VK paths; must keep hearth face access from inheriting node-wide custody. | Mount hearth with only A: A succeeds, direct B identity/archive access fails; lock leaves only F plus whatever separately ruled place S. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:819:| ''CLI opening node session'' (`sealed-act-door.ts:1-21`; `custody-door.ts:2-26`; `stable-founding-road.mem:201`) | CLI owns no vessel S; addressed face rows are D, public verbs F. | Node unlock at most once/boot if S needs it; every CLI run proves its own face; CLI exit doesn't clear daemon boot state. | Offline CLI cannot silently cache VK or reuse previous face admission. | Admit A, then forge/omit B binding through CLI; A operations succeed, B operations refuse; receipts/logs contain no credentials or key bytes. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:832:* ''MEASURED (yours-alone):'' Apple says iOS background extension pages are nonpersistent, may unload, and must save/restore state from storage. This supports re-opening after lifecycle loss, not assuming a live worker as a custody holder. [[Apple Safari extension guidance|https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safariservices/optimizing-your-web-extension-for-safari?changes=_5]], accessed 2026-10-19.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:843:''MEASURED (confirmed-by-both):'' K15 owns one identity/store/registry/archive/content-key seat per PersonaGroup; step 6 moves identity bytes, split stores and archive format together (`stable-founding-road.mem:203,456`; `keyhive-per-persona-group-2026.mem:55-72`). F6 slice three moves Repo/kernel into browser holder, routes sealed writes to asker, and lands with K15 step 3 so each face's custody rows seal under its own key (`stable-founding-road.mem:504-507`). B1 is the browser one-face/custody work referenced by prior handback (`../PRIOR-YIN.md` and `../PRIOR-YANG.md`, 2026-10-19); the exact B1 source lines were not re-opened in this pass, so treat that label as inherited rather than newly measured.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:845:''LEAD sequencing:'' K15.1 define exhaustive row schema and independent FCK/slot/recovery tree; K15.2 enforce per-face identity ownership and split mixed carriers; K15.3 bind browser tab/session and node session to one face, apply (a′), land F6 slice three with authenticated occupied-row replacement; K15.4 remove one face and its rows without sibling rotation; K15.5 one-face recovery/restore; K15.6 migrate identity bytes/stores/FCK routes/archive in one fence. F6 routes writes over established key ownership; it cannot create isolation over VK. Keep Herm's private place signer decision and container no-human restart behavior explicit prerequisites. `sealed-writer.ts:208-218,279-309` shows current occupied-row replacement authenticates existing ciphertext and verifies before rename; preserve that refusal/atomicity in the face writer.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:863:# ''Critical ruling:'' approve the private place signing seed as a separately named floor S (then amend “floor holds no vessel key” precisely), or move it behind a named custody door and accept that a herm's no-face public service changes. Current code is clear-file and auto-load; neither handback's browser finding nor the node SK settles this.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:866:# Exact native-shell custody and guest-owned persistent store are not measured; treat the latter as separate LarVessel if it appears.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:886:''MEASURED:'' Node founding currently mints a vessel key (VK), serving key (SK), and custody root; SK is wrapped by the VK entry in `sk-slots.bin`. Unlock opens VK then SK and holds both; lock drops them. `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-session.ts:80-116,154-190,227-242`; `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-holder.ts:151-155`. The carrier table says the serving class is for rows sealed under SK, but explicitly reports that ''no serving row stands yet'': `packages/lararium-node/src/vault-carriers.ts:12-14,249-251`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:890:''Verdict — LEAD, with a material exception to the earlier handback's broad “no node S” candidate:'' SK is a *secret key by nature*, but it is ''not a current Herm S row'', because there is no serving payload for it to protect and no Herm call site that consumes it. It cannot be made F: the canon says future serving rows are confidential, independently sealed under SK, with a serving gate distinct from both floor and sovereign gates (`bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody.mem:27,40-49`; `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:188,214`). Nor should SK be replaced by the Herm's place key: place identity and serving-row custody have distinct scopes. If a future serving row lands, it creates a genuine node-local S class and requires the row's own serving authorization.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:892:''MEASURED exception:'' The node already has a distinct private *place signing seed* (`vesselSeed`), read from a clear keypair file at boot. It signs as the vessel/place and derives public-floor gate children; it is explicitly distinct from the PersonaGroup root. `packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts:296-314,340-348,429-487,491-499`; carrier table calls `vessel-key` a floor row (`vault-carriers.ts:239-248`); Herm composition receives the seed at `open-node-vessel.ts:3283`. Its public half/card/inception are F, but the private seed itself is confidential and not F. ''LEAD classification: this place key is an existing node-only S'', opened by the daemon at each boot without a human typing or touching anything today. It must be named separately from VK: current usage proves it cannot simply be erased or moved into a face FCK. This is exactly where the abstract law needs a node-specific clause: “floor has no VK” remains true, but “floor is only public material” is false for current node code. To meet the agreed custody law, either protect this S under a narrowly named node boot custody mechanism, or explicitly accept and document the present clear-at-rest place-seed exception; do not disguise it as public F. Thus the node has S today even though no serving S row is measured. The code's SK is redundant for current Herm behavior and must not be conflated with this place-key S.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:901:''LEAD — lock (reconciled):'' Every private record attributable to a PersonaGroup dissolves into that face's rows (D), sealed by that face's independently random FCK and opened only by that face's own slot tree. A floor contains intentionally public/bootstrap/routing material (F), never a VK; any private node place key is separately named S, never relabeled F. A vessel may have an S set only where an inventoried confidential cross-face/system payload cannot be dissolved into D or made public by design; name each row, its owning principal, and its boot-opening mechanism. Browser tabs ask separately per face; CLI and MCP calls present their own face/session at the node gate. Current node daemon opens its place signing seed automatically at boot (an existing, unresolved S exception); any VK-protected node S additionally requires the node's once-per-boot custody unlock. No clock chooses an owner or expires an unlock. The final browser tab leaves browser floor only; node shutdown/restart drops volatile face and serving keys and returns to floor, while persistent place S is available again to the next boot under current code.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:903:The two prior handbacks' current-row census remains authoritative: founding/roster/identity/archive/handle-book/dyad/join/recovery/rotation/clear-custody are mixed current carriers, but the private pieces are D and the deliberately public pieces F; no browser S was found. Their file:line evidence and D/F/S assignments are in `../PRIOR-YIN.md` sections “Census of current vessel-common carriers and acts” and `../PRIOR-YANG.md` section “Census — each currently vessel-common row act.” Node carrier classes are measured at `packages/lararium-node/src/vault-carriers.ts:239-398`; those current placements do not establish target necessity.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:912:The type list below combines canon's one LarVessel/four-host/no-subclass rule (`bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/lar-vessel.mem:20,34`), device-seat matrix (`bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/device-capabilities-2026.mem:129-143`), node classes, and the named planned surfaces. For each, “rows” means the shared census above, filtered to rows that surface can actually hold. `S = ∅` refers to an additional shared *custody payload* after the named place signing seed; current VK wrapping of mixed node rows is not endorsed as target placement. The place signing seed is an extant, separate node S exception detailed below.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:915:| ''Node daemon, Lararium/full node'' | Can host all node rows in the prior census: face roots, archives, roster/maps, joins, dyads, handle-book, recovery and outbox-related records → ''D'' by PersonaGroup; public vessel card/charter/floor route data → ''F''; serving rows → ''S only if actually instantiated''. Current hot/cold carrier table: `vault-carriers.ts:287-398`; each boot starts with empty custody holder: `main.ts:336-345,371-374`. | ''Conditional S:'' extant nonempty serving payload only (none measured in current table: `vault-carriers.ts:12-14`). Operator uses face route at `lares vault unlock` once per boot if the target node S class exists; process lock/restart zero-fills keys and composes floor (`custody-holder.ts:18-27,151-155`; `main.ts:462-469`). | Today the single VK is ancestor to mixed rows. Must partition by face and define an SK owner/route before implementing S. Daemon outputs and receipt/log surfaces must not leak typed credentials (`custody-frames.ts:6-23,37`). | With only face A unlocked, direct carrier open/replace/restore/rotation of B must fail and preserve B bytes; floor and public service still boot with no VK; if S rows exist, VK unlock opens only those node rows and no B row. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:916:| ''Hearth composition'' | Same node store/census as full node; hearth is a lift over the floor, not a new vessel type. Face rows D, public foundation/gate rows F, serving rows conditional S. `main.ts:353-374`; canon `vessel-caps.mem:139-143`. | Same conditional node S; once-per-boot node door; shutdown/lock returns to floor. | A face-bearing hearth needs face admission after node custody unlock; do not treat “node unlocked” as opening every PersonaGroup. Existing implementation binds composition to VK, so target face separation remains work. | Unlock A and mount hearth: read/write A succeeds; B direct row access and B Keyhive/archive appearance fail; lock returns hearth to public floor without losing public serving. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:917:| ''Herm / crossroads node'' | Place signing seed = ''S'' (private node-only identity, auto-loaded at boot); public verifying key/inception/card/charter and public crossroads/read-face/CAS bytes = ''F''; no held PersonaGroup means no face rows to hold. Future recognized operator data must be D under that operator, never retained as Herm face rows. No serving S row currently: `vault-carriers.ts:12-14`. | Place S auto-opens by process boot today, no human prompt (`node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442`; `open-node-vessel.ts:3283`). There is no current SK/serving-row unlock. Raise uses a recognized operator's own authority and ends at causal boundary/reboot (`main.ts:558-575,604-614`). | Herm cannot seat a face (`personaSlotCeiling` fixed 0). Place S is a measured exception to “floor all public.” Future herm serving rows would add separate S; do not substitute place key for SK. | Boot Herm with zero faces: place signing/read/public carriage works; assert no VK or SK prompt/data opens, no face row is written, and place seed never appears in public output. Reboot preserves only place identity and public floor, not raised caps or face keys. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:918:| ''CLI seat opening a node session'' | CLI is not a separate LarVessel; it addresses node-owned rows through the socket. Face-scoped commands/backup/recovery are ''D'' to addressed face; public commands are ''F''; CLI holds no vessel S. `packages/lares-cli/src/sealed-act-door.ts:1-21`; `custody-door.ts:2-26`; node frames `custody-frames.ts:135-202`. | ''S = ∅ at CLI.'' Human types node credential only for node unlock (one per boot); each CLI invocation proves its own face/session at gate, no repeat custody prompt. The terminal does not keep keys after the node's lock/shutdown. Roadmap explicitly says each CLI run proves face: `stable-founding-road.mem:201`. | An offline CLI cannot use node-held row keys unless it explicitly receives face recovery material; it must not cache VK or turn successful prior command into implicit cross-face session. | Unlock node as A; invoke CLI under A and then forge/omit/swap face binding for B. A works; every B operation refuses; inspect CLI receipt/daemon outputs for credential bytes and key material—any appearance fails. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:921:| ''Node daemon inside harbor / civic / mesh-scenarios'' | Same node D/F/S; place signing seed remains S; container packaging changes lifecycle, not row ownership. `stable-founding-road.mem:56,68,104-109`; seed read `node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442`. | Place S auto-opens each process boot today; any future VK-protected S needs explicit once-per-boot custody door. Container restart returns face/serving keys to floor, but current clear-at-rest place seed remains. | Distinguish daemon restart from CLI/MCP client restart. Orchestrator must not auto-unlock face or serving S without human. | Unattended restart restores place identity/public floor but no face/SK custody; every face/serving operation refuses until authorized node unlock. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:936:| ''Android phone leaf / WebAPK'' | D/F/empty S; per-tab face ask; WebAPK still face custody. `device-capabilities-2026.mem:138`. | Do not promote Android Direct Boot/platform storage to cross-face Lares key without an explicit named S row. Red: reboot and verify public floor only, all face roots locked. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:939:| ''Native/desktop shell (planned)'' | Same D/F/empty S absent explicit local system secret; each shell session face unlock; last shell session drops face keys. Roadmap names desktop/browser app boundary at `stable-founding-road.mem:68,104-109`; no native-shell storage row was verified. | OS keychain integration would add a custody mechanism, not alter row owner. Red: another OS account/shell session cannot open face ciphertext without that face's slot route. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:948:For every row-bearing node/container type above, acts are filtered from the merged census: (1) found place / VK / slot tree → place signing seed ''S'' under today's implementation; public place/card/charter F; each PersonaGroup root/FCK/slot tree D; serving key/tree only becomes S if a serving payload is actually present; (2) fleet offer/join pending → public signed transport F, target face's pending secret/address/record D; (3) slot bind/remove/recovery → that face's route tree D; (4) roster, labels, declarations, handle-book → face-specific content D, minimal opaque public routing only F; (5) Keyhive/Veil archive, dyads, face proof/member and Nexus keys → D; (6) face backup/restore → D; (7) clear custody removes that face's rows and routes, while F survives; (8) floor card, public charter, public gate and public artifact carriage → F. Prior precise carrier/caller citations: `../PRIOR-YIN.md` census table and `../PRIOR-YANG.md` census table. Node carrier line inventory: `vault-carriers.ts:287-398`; rotation's current VK-carrier sweep: `vault-carriers.ts:477-510` (current mechanic to be replaced by face/row-aware rotation).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:957:''MEASURED:'' Node's current process starts with an empty custody holder (`main.ts:336-345`); vault unlock opens node custody, and `custody-holder.ts:151-155` holds VK/SK until lock. ''LEAD target:'' retain the one-per-boot node unlock only for a named node S set; then every CLI/MCP/watcher invocation proves its own face as the roadmap directs. If S is empty, node starts and remains at floor without asking anything. Container supervisors never turn restart policy into key custody; restart is a causal boundary that drops volatile keys. No wall clock, last-seen timer, or silent orchestrator retry may select a face owner.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:966:# `herm` has no current serving rows and no current SK consumer at raise. Future ember serving rows are canonically planned but not yet represented in the carrier table; thus there is no current Herm *serving-key* S. The place signing seed is a different, current Herm S loaded at boot. `vault-carriers.ts:12-14`; `custody.mem:49,80,98`; `node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:990:| Browser has one VK tree mixing face and vessel carriers today. | ''CONFIRM, scoped to the named custody rows.'' `packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-custody.ts:2-12,54-68,386-402` has one `custody-slots` tree and uses VK for those rows. This says nothing about unrelated content encryption. | confirmed-by-both |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:996:| Container restart may silently restore face/SK unlock for availability. | ''REFUTE as target.'' Restart drops volatile custody and leaves F; without an explicit human boot authorization, any D or future S is locked. Container wiring is deployment, not authority. `main.ts:336-345,427-430`; `founding-runbook.mem:156`; container entrypoint cited in MINE. | yours-alone |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:997:| CLI and MCP inherit whichever node face last unlocked. | ''REFUTE.'' CLI is a seat against node's socket and must provide act/session authority; roadmap says each CLI run proves face. `sealed-act-door.ts:1-21`, `custody-door.ts:13-30`, `stable-founding-road.mem:201`; MCP wire only configures a session (`codex-wire.ts:70-93`). | yours-alone |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:1009:''MEASURED:'' The node-wide custody tree currently wraps VK to SK, then keeps both in process memory (`custody-session.ts:80-116,154-190,227-242`; `custody-holder.ts:151-155`). Carrier classification is implementation, not target necessity. There are no serving rows today (`vault-carriers.ts:12-14`). The exception TWIN did not see is the independently loaded place signing seed. It cannot be called F because it is a private signing capability; it also cannot be collapsed into the future serving key. The house must decide whether to protect this key behind a narrow node boot custody door or accept a documented clear-at-rest S exception. The current code auto-opens it on each daemon boot, without a human gesture. This means the strict candidate law “all floor material is public” needs exactly one present-day bend; “floor holds no VK” remains intact.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:1013:For every node/container/seat type in the previous table, common acts filter as follows (''MEASURED current carriers; LEAD target rows''): founding place signing seed is S on node (public verifying half/card/charter F); PersonaGroup root, FCK and slot tree D; fleet public signed offer/answer F while target-face pending secret/address/join record D; face slot changes/recovery D; private roster, labels, handle-book/recognition graph D while minimal public opaque routes F only after leakage review; Keyhive/Veil archives, dyads, proof/member/Nexus keys D; per-face backup/restore D; clear-custody removes only that face's D and leaves F; future serving rows S only when instantiated and named. The carrier/caller evidence appears in `../PRIOR-YIN.md` and `../PRIOR-YANG.md` census tables and `packages/lararium-node/src/vault-carriers.ts:287-398`; archive row selector remains unresolved.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:1030:| Probe (Mudlet or other outbound seat) | Probe holds no face custody S and no FCK; addressed node rows remain D/F there; ''S=∅ at probe''. It presents a face/session to node for each call. | Red: with A admitted, ask probe for B row; node refuses, no key material is cached in probe. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face.mem:1033:| Node daemon / full Lararium | D all PersonaGroup records; F public place card/charter/routing; S includes current private place signing seed plus only future named serving payloads. Face sessions present per act; node custody door, if retained for other S, opens once per boot. Restart/shutdown clears volatile VK/SK/FCK; current persistent place seed auto-loads next boot. | Red: one-face node unlock cannot open sibling carriers; fresh restart has no face/serving keys; public floor works and only narrowly named place identity survives. |
