/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/l-space.mem:32:* ''the apophatic center'' (//neti-neti//, "not this, not this") — a center named only by negation, where stripping predicates leaves ''presence, not void''. L-Prime made mechanical: each copula removed strips one false predicate from the center.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/l-space.mem:46:The ''dead sink below'' names thermodynamic equilibrium — the static fixed point a relation //relaxes into// when it freezes. A bare `X ${copula} Y` reads as a trajectory sliding downhill: it fuses a live relation into static identity, draining toward dead water. ''The copula is the gradient down; L-Prime is the through-flux that holds the center metastable'' above its own sink. The discipline reads thermodynamic, not merely stylistic: cut the active-voice flux and the address relaxes into essence-static, the center falling into the sink.
