/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:34:> ''Register.'' The operator ruled the browser's first proof (operator ruling, 2026-10-11; quote license: //"Approve your lean on the browser first-proof carrier."//). The per-vessel custody shape stands adopted by the house under the operator's standing grant; the operator read it and overruled nothing. The remainder reads as ''the designed shape''. #/owed names what stays unproven, and a builder MUST NOT harden an unproven part into code as law.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:43:| Vessel roots and custody key | each vessel mints its own (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lararium-identity#/vessel-key">>) | that vessel's custody | no gate proof and no sibling proof contains it |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:44:| Persona root | the founding vessel mints it; the root holder controls its authority acts | the root holder's custody alone; it never travels | an authorized private reader of the PersonaGroup may verify its public authority history; no gate receives its edge |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:46:| ''A vessel's face-scoped key'', one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus, vessel) | the joined vessel mints it at random; the face key certifies it ONCE, at the join | that vessel's custody; its trusted daemon invokes it | a gate sees it and its certificate inside the encrypted exchange |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:50:| Gate bundle | the gate derives separate, domain-separated transport and signing keys per (tier, Nexus, route): a floor route's from the floor key, a serving route's from the serving key, a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (#/the-gate-exchange) | nowhere: a bundle lives in memory from a derivation to a drop; a dialer pins it per (Nexus, route) | the dialer, and anyone handed the pin |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:112:> ''Operator ruling, approved as presented; it touches custody at rest.''
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:114:''A route names its tier, and a tier names its root.'' A ''floor route'' answers at a locked vessel: the public shelf, the oracle's read face, the floor's announcement, and a herm's blind relay of bytes it cannot open. Its bundle derives from the floor key. A ''sovereign route'' seats a face's session, syncs a private document or serves a lane whose bytes this vessel can open. Its bundle derives from the sealed custody root, and it exists only while the vessel stands unlocked. A route's typed name carries its tier, the pin states it and the pin's digest binds it: no route asks the other tier's root, a root asked for the wrong tier refuses by name, and a dialer that pinned one tier believes no gate of the other.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:126:> ''House ruling under the operator's delegation'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/rulings">>); it reopens on proof that a gate pin decides no authority anywhere.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:128:''A serving route answers at a vessel its embers raised to SERVING'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember">>): the serving gate for presenters already standing, and blind carriage for them. Its bundle derives from the serving key under its own registered domain, and it exists only while the vessel stands at SERVING or unlocked. The floor and sovereign tiers stand untouched: no serving route asks the floor key or the custody root, and a dialer that pinned the sovereign tier believes no serving gate. A serving gate signs its own handshake and no act, and its seat reaches what the serving tier holds and nothing beyond it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:200:* ''A household TLS terminator, its log's reader, or a herm that sees the upgrade, once it holds candidate sovereign gate pins, learns which Nexus a dial selects among the K gates sharing its address and route (at most log2(K) bits per dial, none where K=1) and links that Nexus's repeat visits; the knock never tells it the presenting face, the admission verdict or any sealed byte.'' The operator's ruling of 2026-10-26 places this reader outside the sovereign route's promise. A sovereign pin escaping its members' custody, or a ruling that extends route confidentiality to pin-holders, reopens `W10` (the reading and its measurements stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane">> #/the-knock-reading).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:359:* ''Two custody rows.'' The face proof key rests cold with the root holder, one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus); a vessel's face-scoped key rests hot on its own vessel, one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus). Each holds 32 secret bytes and reads whole or refuses by name. The modules name the rows and the two signing doors they ask of the custody seat, and write no row.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:360:* ''The admit's own mark.'' The supplier reads the presenter-verifier's verdict over an admit and checks it against the chain. The admit's quorum signs a commitment to what it carries (`carriageCommit`), and the held-root door hands back the head of the admitted nym's key line, which the supplier holds against the chain's face key; the verdict itself still carries no mark a caller cannot spell by hand. A chain another vessel presented verifies as well as this vessel's own, so the session opener also owes the supplier the key its own custody row names.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:363:* ''The floor and sovereign roots' doors'' stand at their seats (the serving key's door stands owed with train E), and no composer calls them until the socket cutover. A floor bundle asks the floor key's derive door (`vesselFloorKeyDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`), which answers while the vessel rests locked, hands back a fresh child its caller overwrites and never the floor key. A sovereign bundle asks the custody seat's (`custodyGateDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-seat.ts`), which answers only while the seat holds its key. The two doors carry two types, so a line that hands one tier's door to the other fails to compile; a root refuses a door of the other tier and a door no mint made by name (`door-other-tier`); and each seat's door refuses the other tier's child by name. A door states only what its minter claimed, so one weld holds the minters to the two seats: a second caller of either mint, anywhere in source, turns it red (`packages/lararium-node/tests/gate-root-door-minters.test.ts`). The composer owes the call.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:364:* ''Sealed rows for the gate's memory'' stand at the custody seat, and no gate calls them until the socket cutover. The store asks a door for one row of bytes by name (`gateMemoryRows`, `packages/lararium-node/src/gate-memory-rows.ts`): one row per face key in the vessel's storage home, named by the proof-subject digest, sealed under the vessel key through the seat's one-holder update door. One holder answers one door, so the gates of one composition share one writer; and a write that lacks an event the row holds refuses while the row keeps its bytes. A locked vessel reads none and refuses by name; a row that stands and does not open, or opens to anything but a list of events, refuses at the read and at the write, its bytes never move, and the gate that asked falls silent. The store drops its view of a row whose write the door refused and verifies that row again. The seat holds no counter a restored disk could not also restore, so the door adds no fence against a rollback (#/the-withdrawal-proof). The row belongs to its vessel, and no face's backup bundle carries it. The composer owes the call.
