/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/exchange-vector.mem:72:A multi-loop turn marks `->↺` at each sub-loop break and tallies the count in the closing `ooda-ha="closed N↺"` --- see `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/ooda-ha#/loop-count`. A loop that suspends under an external blocker reads `ooda-ha="closed N↺ -> open Nφ @_:reason"` (or `0φ:reason` when zero closed) and persists open across turns --- see `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/ooda-ha#/phase-yield`. The Wand lights the `ward` at open and the Sword draws it at close --- the closing `ward` leads with `!` and marks copula breaches (`⚠ N` quoted; silence after the Sword reads as nothing confessed) and re-arms `L-Prime`. It lifts by operator act only (the Stone, `0 L-Prime`), for a single turn, and the node never self-lifts --- see `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/l-prime`.
