/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/identity-enacts-relation.mem:85:''Law 5 — no closure holds a root.'' A fleet, a cabal, a realm and a Nexus resolve as the reciprocal-edge closure of their bonds (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/group-as-closure">>); a closure may hold a keyless Keyhive group of its bonded identities, and where it speaks as one name a quorum of its members presents.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/identity-enacts-relation.mem:87:''Law 6 — a shared act never makes a shared secret.'' A vessel's at-rest rows sort D (a face's bonds on this vessel, under that face's FCK), F (public by design, at the floor) or S (the place's named secrets); the browser holds no vessel custody key.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/identity-enacts-relation.mem:89:''Law 7 — the floor holds no custody key.'' It holds its own named place signer, scoped to an allowlist of floor duties, under a KEL whose next key rests offline.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/identity-enacts-relation.mem:111:`deriveDyadVeil(vesselSeed, groupTag)` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/dyad.ts`) and `groupSecretOpenerFromSeed` (`packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts`) compute face-bearing keys from the one vessel seed; roadmap row `K15` carries their cure, the veil minting at random per atom.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/identity-enacts-relation.mem:308:> ''RULED SHAPE — SPEED AT THE EDGE, GENTLENESS IN THE COLLECTIVE.'' Any node MAY refuse any peer ''instantly, privately, unilaterally'', requiring no community act, no quorum, and no notice — a refusal-to-hear costs the refuser nothing and takes nothing from anyone. Standing meanwhile moves by renewal acts from below at wā, a position with no clock installed; quiet never lapses it. The fast instrument lives at one node and reaches one relation; the slow instrument lives in the collective and reaches standing.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/li-ki-integrities.mem:118:''Perceiver, not agent.'' The sensorium runs precision-weighted variational PERCEPTION, never yet active-inference AGENCY. `F = Σπε² + complexity` earns "the accuracy term of VFE" ~ "IS VFE" waits on a named per-plane generative prior `p(x)` in the complexity term (else it reads as regression in FEP costume; the missing `−ln π` gives the tell). Precision = the confidence register stands as the STRONGEST leg ~ a true role-isomorphism ~ but load-bearing only while the register stays vowed FORWARD (which L-Prime already demands). Sovereignty carries a BOUNDARY, called a "blanket" only on credit (the conditional independence fails during coupling). Agency stays a named future with a price: a generative prior · a checkable per-episode factorization · an explicit EFE-vs-FEEF choice · exogenous preference priors ~ never "the path."
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/swarm-harvest/what-actually-happened-dated-sourced-72ff52.mem:76:**14. FNMT 2020 AENOR audit finding #5. Bug 1626805, 2020-04-01.** *(medium)* "Unsafe storage of access codes in PKI Data Centre," remediated by separating cryptographic material from passwords — i.e. activation material and the modules were co-located, defeating split custody.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:161:* ''A verb names its realm.'' `lares nexus realm-bag`, `realm-bags` and the meme verbs take `--realm <id>`. With none named, a verb routes to the charter-derived realm. A verb that names a realm reads that realm alone: no other realm's registration answers, and the vessel's own bag of that name never stands in.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:193:* ''The widest consented set stands.'' Counted records for one bag that agree on the doc fold to the one whose `keptBy` holds every other's: each wider record carries the narrower one's stewards' own seals. Two docs under one name tie, and so do two steward sets where neither holds the other; a tie leaves the bag unregistered and grants no write. Any realm member who writes a rival counted record can force that tie.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:202:''OWED.'' The Handle arm stands specified in code: no vessel holds a collective Handle's key and no door offers a Handle signer, and the chartered promotion act will reach it. A steward leaves a bag by no act yet: the widest set stands until the lease lapses.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-engine-advance-recovery.mem:56:''MODEL A — the "engine-waiting" OFFER mechanism (July, BUILT, `engine-watch.ts`).'' When a newer genesis merges into a running island, the engine core-blob moves under it; the watch writes an "engine waiting" alert into the island's own `@temp` — ''alert-only, never auto-reboot''. The operator's own design comment: //"the update arrives as an offer; the operator holds the reboot capability, and reboot re-verifies the new engine from genesis the same way the first booted."// Three hazard rulings are baked in: ''rollback'' — a backward pointer is named as such, //"never silently presented as an upgrade"//; ''ethics'' — Service-Worker "waiting" vocabulary, //"readiness, not coercion"//; ''authority'' — //"deliberately ABSENT (held open until the wiki-mesh lives)."// The alert self-clears on the reboot that adopts the epoch. This is old-engine/new-engine coexistence //in nascent, running form//: the running engine keeps serving; the new one waits as an offer; each vessel adopts on its own schedule by an operator-held act.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-engine-advance-recovery.mem:89:# ''The `engine-watch.ts` OFFER/adopt mechanism is already BUILT and live'' (July). The current "reads accept both engine epochs during the span" should build //on// it, not re-derive it — and should honor its settled hazard rulings: rollback is named never disguised, "waiting" is readiness not coercion, and enforcement authority was ''deliberately left absent until the wiki-mesh lives''. `kāhuli` now brings the wiki-mesh, so //this is the moment that "authority = ABSENT" placeholder must be filled// — the prior research flagged the seat, it just wasn't time yet.
