/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/sensorium-machina.mem:527:The producer's exact bytes and their positions enter custody before any parser speaks. A parser's block ''occurrence'' binds source, immutable byte revision, parser identity and position; a separate digest witnesses the emitted text. An observation says which revision a source exposed at a named horizon. A typed ledger records that interpretation without turning its block key into a content hash. An owned Content view then projects those blocks under an explicit model identity and a separate completion frontier. The names keep retry, reparse, duplicate text and A→B→A honest without making a parser output stand in for the original bytes.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lararium-identity.mem:139:''"Leaf" names a RELATION contracted at the second layer, never a vessel that holds fewer roots.'' A browser that serves as a leaf of its human's node Lararium still holds its own vessel roots. Standing lives in the relation: a browser that loses its storage and recovers no vessel secret stands as a NEW vessel with new roots and contracts in again, and nothing above the vessel layer gets lost with it (the recovery products stand apart at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/secure-context#/custody-leans">>).
