/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/pattern-integrities-cultural.mem:142:''Shape:'' place-bound record + federated custody with no global copy + constitutionally external witness. Roughly half the Lares architecture, running for millennia, never written down — by design.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/pattern-integrities-cultural.mem:216:''P10 songlines → federation gating + non-reflexive witness.'' Segment custody with no global copy maps onto the membrane law (local supervised caps; only meshpalace federates; never ambient). The kirda/kurdungurlu rule maps onto C3 operationally: the party that owns a result cannot solely certify it — the witness sits in the complementary line. Rule: every federated claim carries a witness-seat structurally outside its owner.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/working-procedures.mem:134:* ''Check `pgrep -af vitest` and `pgrep -af witness` before a run that stages vessels''; bisect a red in a worktree, never by guessing. A lone red that clears standalone names suspect shared state before it names a defect.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/working-procedures.mem:168:* ''Vocabulary law'': OCI nouns name structure and residency verbs name motion; a version-control verb MUST NOT name a model operation. `ea` names the breath, never a "heartbeat"; `nalu` names the wave. Web2 vocabulary reads as crud. Prose in `api/` and in a spirit's own telling keeps L-Prime (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/l-prime">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/working-procedures.mem:172:* ''Early alpha, until a third human'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). Shapes get tried and thrown away freely while one or two operators hold the mesh, since that takes only minimal coordination. Once a third human's data and habits enter it, and in any stable federated mesh, human-scale flows and persistence become the primary design attractors. The road's fence (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/rulings">>) reads the same line.
