/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:16:role              = "dreamdom-roadmap — a roadmap to the DreamDOM: the phased build order from today's as-built worker-thread VM to the full superset of cameras the `dreamdom` carrier models. One train, D, in eight phases (D0 measure and mend · D1 the camera contract at width none · D2 the record port · D3 the glass engine and the width spike · D4 the Wiki Actor · D5 conformance · D6 the lean sinks · D7 the wider surfaces), each with what it builds, what it proves (witnesses and goldens), what it waits on, the spikes that gate it and the open rulings that block it; the lanes named the way the house roadmap names them; the spikes and rulings gathered; the rows beside the phase that closes each; what stands off this road by ruling. Reads under `stable-founding-road#/the-attractor` and the lane law of `controller-handoff`."
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:28:''What this carrier holds.'' The build order from today's worker-thread TiddlyWiki (one engine per island, whole HTML frames to a shadow root, a render-id relay back) to the full model `dreamdom` carries: four layers, two waists, a camera as a root over a sink, a width dial, a Wiki Actor, and every surface of the superset publishing its own conformance row. Each phase names what it builds, what it proves, what it waits on, the spikes that gate it and the rulings that block it. Landed work will read in git and the CHANGELOG, never here; this carrier keeps only what stays owed, and the controller trues it as rows close.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:32:''The lane law binds every lane here'' (`controller-handoff#/the-lane-law`): one lead per lane in its own worktree; red first, with a control; a race pinned by the product's own event; suites from source under a scratch `HOME` and a scratch `LAR_ROOT` with `LAR_BAGS` unset; a plugin or tiddler change rebuilds the bundle in the same commit and declares its gap in `genesis/unbaked.json`; never a boot in the tracked tree; a refused command stops the lane; a burst, then one shard, then `MERGE-VERIFY`; canon lines in each commit, L-Prime kept.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:87:* ''Owed'': the whole-road Playwright run of the goldens over a staged vessel (the two harnesses stand in for it: the engine half over the fake document, the page half over the real sink with a stand-in island); `glass-switch-back-repaints` and `glass-print-refuses-by-name` as e2e witnesses; probes 2 and 4 of `page-controls#/measure-first`, and probes 1 and 5 in Gecko and WebKit; long animation frames across 100 edits on the vessel page (D0's observer); the page consuming the scroll and focus hints; `lar:disclosure-toggle` for disclosure state the wiki keeps; a `lar:breath` kind so the plate reads the island's breath after boot; the daemon surface's breath, custody and residency records (`daemon-surface#/the-talk-story`); the `data-lar-keys` stamp from `$edit-text`'s `parseKeyDescriptors`; the operator's own renames of `wiki:place-verb`, `daemon:*`, `cas:*` and `view:*`, deferred by their word.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:93:* ''Rulings'' (`dreamdom#/open-rulings`, ruled 2026-10-16): the stock edit template through the seam engine, each width naming what it cannot run; the root `tm-*` split, with `tm-http-request` as a gated door; `$eventcatcher` for declared discrete events and `$keyboard` with declared keys.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:96:* ''Builds'': the port's kinds on the live island: `port:open{wikiUri, width, since, actor, localFilter, renders[], edits, presence, maxRecordBytes, maxBatchBytes}`, `port:snapshot` (chunked), `port:changes` with cursors and tombstones, `port:write{txId, basis, records}` answered by `port:written` and echoed under `causedBy:[txId]`, `port:ask{kind: filter · render · load · verb · cas · invoke}` where `render` answers `html` · `text` · `blocks` (with `affordances[]`) · `label-html` and `invoke` carries a `renderCursor`, `port:presence` (lapse by presence rounds at causal boundaries, never persisted), `port:close`; the width field as a filter over fields on the engine side (cheap now, expensive to retrofit); the tier `localFilter` naming StoryList, HistoryList, `$:/state`, `$:/temp`, `$:/status` and `$:/info/browser/*`; a recording fakedom-style document and the blocks, text and label-html serialisers over it; the capability gate on every invoke before `invokeActions`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:102:* ''Rulings'' (`dreamdom#/open-rulings`, ruled 2026-10-16): presence at width none travels as a separate droppable message. The port ships with `causedBy` mandatory and skinny behind a flag.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:112:* ''Rulings'' (`dreamdom#/open-rulings`): the `§9` wording and the confirm road's home per width stand ruled (2026-10-16); the default width of the first surface stays open until the three-boot spike reads. The flag ships first; the default flips after.
