/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/two-way-interaction-scout.mem:16:role              = "two-way-interaction-scout — VERBATIM handoff of a tasked Fable spirit (2026-10-16): how the DreamDOM superset keeps the full two-way interaction between a person at a surface and the wiki. Carries the inventory of every TiddlyWiki interaction by widget, message and layer with its owner, up-leg and down-leg per width and host; the up-leg contract (wiki:control-event, declared-at-mount stamps, reliable acts against droppable senses, wake on act, two surfaces on one actor); the silent-loss risks with their fixes or refusals; interaction goldens with fourteen scripts; the ten-surface two-way table; Mu, two stories, spikes and open rulings. Held as a collision surface; dreamdom carries the house's reading of it."
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/two-way-interaction-scout.mem:43:Lares (Artificer) · Fable, tasked spirit · 2026-10-16. Research pass for the operator's charge: *"Now we need to ensure the 2-way interaction is preserved."* Frame: `third-ways.md` (the map after the rulings) and `model-and-gaps.md` (the as-built survey). Inputs read whole: the boot seed; `dreamdom.mem` (#/the-ruling, #/the-layers, #/the-question, #/what-a-replacement-un-skips, #/the-vectors), `page-controls.mem`, `session-contract.mem#/the-holder-protocol`, `vm-projection-bus.mem`, `render-pipeline.mem#/render-posture`, `wikispace-canvasspace-ontology.mem#/the-surface-law`; `packages/lararium-web/src/projection-sink.ts`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/{tw5-camera,tw5-projection,has-island-watches}.ts`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/island-protocol.ts` (the two DOM kinds); the TiddlyWiki5 submodule at `ea94ca8` (5.5.0-prerelease fork, checked out in `/home/user/gjd5`): `widgets/{widget,button,link,checkbox,radio,select,range,browse,dropzone,droppable,draggable,keyboard,eventcatcher,navigator,dialog,reveal,list,scrollable,action-*}.js`, `editor/{factory,engines/simple,engines/framed}.js`, `editor/operations/text/*`, `utils/dom/{popup,scroller,modal,notifier,dragndrop,dom}.js`, `utils/fakedom.js`, `utils/confirm.js`, `keyboard.js`, `startup/{rootwidget,story,windows,confirm,startup}.js`, `ui/PageTemplate.tid`, `ui/PageTemplate/story.tid`, `ui/EditTemplate/*`, `wiki/macros/{tag-picker,keyboard-driven-input}.tid`. Nothing edited, nothing booted; no tracked file touched.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/two-way-interaction-scout.mem:47:**A naming ruling folded in (Telarus, 2026-10-16).** The operator pet-names the WHOLE concept **DreamDOM**. The name began as the house's replacement for `$tw.fakeDocument` (`dreamdom.mem#/head`: a document instanced twice with the thread boundary inside it). The concept has since grown: **DreamDOM now names the superset of cameras**, every HTML5-capable device AND every surface the research waves targeted (the browser on the Node vessel's box, any other browser or WebView shell, the Node-served browser and SSR face, QuickJS/Hermes shells, the UE6 sidecar, Mudlet, MCP/chat and others), each a *(root template, document sink)* over the one engine. This report uses the name that way throughout. `dreamdom.mem`'s narrower sense, the two-instance document with tight bindings, now reads as **one member of the superset**: the browser DOM sink at width none, hardened by the page-controls contract. Its rulings (keyed absolute frames, sensed snapshots up, true events queue and get answers, layer 3 belongs to the page, the five `isTiddlyWikiFakeDom` sites as a test roster) carry to every member, since each member faces the same two legs. §7 gives the per-surface table the ruling asked for.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/two-way-interaction-scout.mem:65:7. **Open rulings** (§9): whether a sleeping actor wakes on an act or on a frame request; whether the browser DOM sink keeps the stock edit template over `lar-field` or ships a house edit template; which root `tm-*` services become host-service requests and which refuse; whether `$eventcatcher`/`$keyboard` stay REFUSED at width none or earn a declared-keys binding; the presence lane's home; and the per-surface default width.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/two-way-interaction-scout.mem:152:This section extends `page-controls.mem#/the-wire` (one keyed frame down, one answered event up) and `session-contract.mem#/the-holder-protocol` (`wiki:control-event` → `projection:control-result`; `schemaVersion`, `ownerEpoch`, `sessionId`, `generation`, `surfaceId`, `mountEpoch` on every message). Nothing here reopens the rulings; it fills the fields the roster in §2 showed missing.
