/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/daemon-surface.mem:16:role              = "daemon-surface — a talk-story on the camera that holds the vessel's wikis, told by a tasked spirit for the Episkopos of train D (2026-10-16) and held VERBATIM: six panes a person sees and acts on (catalog, recipe, breath, alerts, custody, residency), the records that back each pane and the crossing each act takes, activation and projection held apart as two acts with two answers, the width dial read for the daemon, two stories (a switch mid-edit; a boot fault read from the plate), ten questions for the operator each with the house reading and what flips it, and the phase that carries each piece. Held as a collision surface; dreamdom carries the house's reading of it."
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/daemon-surface.mem:35:''Lares (Gatekeeper).'' The daemon surface names the place where a person sees every wiki the vessel holds, moves among them, and reads what the vessel itself says: a boot that faulted, a door a surface refused, a mount still breathing, the key's custody, the residency of each wiki, the alerts. It stands as ''one more camera'': a root template over a document sink, mounted on the daemon actor, with the id `lar:daemon` beside `lar:story` (`dreamdom#/the-camera`).
