/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mudlet-scout.mem:16:role              = "mudlet-scout — VERBATIM handoff of a tasked Fable spirit: Mudlet (the Lua 5.1 MUD client) surveyed 2026-10-16 as a host where a lararium joins any game or world as a capability, never as the game. Carries Mudlet's capability surface (Lua, GMCP and its kin, HTTP without WebSocket, Geyser panes, the mapper, packages, the loopback MCP server merged into development), four integration patterns (virtual-MUD projection, proxy, package over HTTP, server-side module), the TiddlyWiki mapping across store, engine and projection, AI co-player squads under wizard approval on Islands of Myth, the sensorium and live-3D deferral, a phased plan riding the portable-engine plan, and seven open rulings. Held as a collision surface."
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mudlet-scout.mem:45:Fable web researcher, tasked spirit, 2026-10-16. Inputs read in full: the boot seed (`noosphere-boot.mem`), `host-attractors.md` (its Mudlet deep dive §5 and the projection-port sketch §2.3–2.4 and §9.2), `portable-engine-plan-v2.md` (the Tiddler Port, `port:ask`, phases and rulings), `model-and-gaps.md`, and the `@lararium/sensorium` package manifest (its README does not exist; the package.json description stood in). `third-ways.md` was left alone. No repository code was read beyond that manifest; nothing in the tree was touched.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mudlet-scout.mem:47:**Reach in this pass.** `WebSearch` answered in both modes. `WebFetch` resolved **only `github.com`** (the Mudlet repository, its releases, pull requests and issues, the Evennia repository, tbaMUD, pycat); two guessed LIMA mudlib URLs on GitHub returned 404. Nothing on wiki.mudlet.org, mudlet.org, forums.mudlet.org, islandsofmyth.org, achaea.com or aardwolf.com was fetched; those claims rest on search-returned passages. No tool was refused outright in this pass. Marks: **[reached: fetched]** the page was read (GitHub only) · **[reached: search]** confirmed through search passages · **[unreached]** memory only, flagged where used · *(inferred)* reasoning, not evidence.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mudlet-scout.mem:67:7. **Phased plan (§9)** rides v2: Phase 1's `port:ask` (filter, render with `label-html`/`text`/`blocks`, load, invoke) is the only thing Mudlet needs from the engine; a GMCP adapter in the node island, a Muddler-built `.mpackage`, a proxy mode and a LIMA-side GMCP module follow. Red/green tests and seven open rulings close the file.
