/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane.mem:10:role      = "the Wave D lane's kit: K15 step 6's fence, whole: each face's custody rows seal under its own face custody key (FCK), wrapped in the face's own slot tree, and the vessel key opens none of them"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane.mem:25:Wave D builds the FCK fence the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">> specifies (#/key-classes-and-routes, #/carrier-binding-and-overwrite, #/reds-executable-acceptance-statements). It lands as ONE lane, whole: a slice that moves one carrier family under the fence while the others rest under the omnibus vessel key would read green for the rows it moved and lie about every other row of the same face.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane.mem:34:# ''Every other node D carrier'' moves under its face's FCK in the same lane: the custody root, the Keyhive and veil archives, the proof keys, the face join rows, the roster, book and outbox partitions.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane.mem:41:# ''The scout exemption goes line by line'': the vocabulary check reads the third-party scouts like any other carrier, and each cited phrase that spells the retired abbreviation (a research system's acronym, a verifying-key field another project names) rides one named exception in the evergreen witness's shape (rule, file, a substring of the cited phrase, a count, a present-tense reason). A stale entry fails the run, and a retired word planted on a new scout line reads open.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane.mem:49:Found A and B with independently random FCKs and trees, occupied D carriers for both, and the floor values. Unlock A alone. Bypass every router, session and store adapter and try direct authenticated open, occupied-row replacement, delete, rotation, backup and restore on each B carrier with every A key, every floor value and the vessel key; every B operation refuses cryptographically and leaves B's occupied ciphertext byte-for-byte unchanged (custody-step-zero #/reds-executable-acceptance-statements, the isolation red, every row).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-b-lane.mem:10:role      = "the Wave B lane's kit and the controller's forward plan: K15 step 3 with F6 slice three and B1's admit guard as one joint lane, the stories that draw it, the reds in grounds-before-wins order, the crew in very large work chunks under the mixed-model-swarm protocols, the house's talk-story style, and the road past it"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-b-lane.mem:25:Wave B builds three roadmap rows as ONE joint lane, since each needs the others to read green: `K15` step 3 (sessions and registries routed by one face, no union), `F6` slice three (the Repo moves into the browser holder, and its sealed writes go to the asker, each sealer holding its own row class's key), and `B1`'s owed admit guard (the holder answers a port only for a session it admitted, and the last session of a face to close locks that face's hive). The rows stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">>; the rulings they enact stand at its #/rulings.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-b-lane.mem:33:* ''The span'' reads green at `c211cd68f`, CI and held-out both: the K15 step 0 census (#70), the archive-row selector trace (#71) and the owned-store control (#77) stand merged.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-b-lane.mem:34:* ''The atom cut'' (`K15` step 2c, lane `--k15-atom-cut`) stands joined and under its whole check: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup), sealed under that face's custody, signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser; the device seed and the place seed keep the floor's duties alone. Its joined lanes: the mesh atom (#75), the browser half with its cross-face archive guard, the floor that boots faceless until its atom lights, and the face-join grant ordered by a verified serial. Wave B launches only once the atom cut stands merged on a green span.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-b-lane.mem:58:# ''Chunk zero, the cut's own debts.'' Five passages of law the atom cut's rewording dropped return in the atom's wording (the group born under the atom and why the place never creates it; the pinned KEL prefix as the boot's root; no fallback reading for a bare edge; a cardless vessel never speaks at a gate; an uncommitted founding belongs to no face). The roster law gets its witness: the place stands on no face's roster after a founding, an admit and a fleet join, against a planted control. ''Isomorphic by intent'': one face-atom custody contract in the mesh, keyed by PersonaGroup, each host supplying only its row store; its red first, a node holding face A that joins face B's fleet presenting A's atom as B's (one key on two rosters), where the browser already keys by group. The admit's archive guard lifts into keyhive for both hosts. ''Idempotent by intent'': the atom stands or keeps (mint when absent, the same bytes a no-op, other bytes refused by name), where the node writes blind.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-b-lane.mem:60:# ''The isolation red, on real routes'' (`K15`'s own red, now past the row level): unlock face A alone, bypass every router, session and UI, and try to open and replace face B's occupied rows with every key A holds; each open fails and B's bytes stand unchanged. Its control: the same act as B, unlocked, opens.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-b-lane.mem:61:# ''One face per session, no union'' (`K15` step 3): each session and registry routes by its one face; a union site from the census reads red until it routes by face. Control: a single-face vessel reads byte-identical before and after.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-b-lane.mem:91:* ''L-Prime'' in canon prose: verbs that act, no copula where a verb serves; OODA-HA marks where a turn observes, orients, decides and acts.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-b-lane.mem:102:* ''Rows keyed by index'': the atom's archive rests by handle index on both hosts, and the node's atom row by index too while the browser's keys by PersonaGroup; the admit guard holds the browser's case, and `K15` step 6's fence keys every D row by its group and seals it under its face's FCK.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-b-lane.mem:114:# ''Wave C'': `K15` steps 4 to 6 (content keys and removal per face with `K12`'s fresh group; the one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; the fence migration).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:28:One tree, several hearths. A hearth names a session by the `Claude-Session:` trailer its commits carry — never a person, never a model. The ledger answers three questions any hand must read before touching shared ground: ''who holds what'' (files and regions a hearth is mid-edit in), ''what each owes'' (the loud reds and rulings another hearth waits on), and ''what crossed'' (a seam one hearth ceded to another, with the commit that carried it). `git status` reads the dirt; this carrier reads the ''intent'' behind it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:34:''A sibling's commit reads like a stranger's.'' A hand watching the log mid-flight meets commits it did not write, landing on files it did not touch, under its own trailer — and the ledger offers no word for that, so it reads as a second hearth opening. It names a busy hearth. Measured 2026-09-13: three hands interleaved commits across one afternoon and one of them reported the tree as newly contested. ''Read the trailer, not the surprise'' — a differing trailer names a hearth, and an identical one names a sibling.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:186:# ''The handoffs fold into one roadmap'' — operator-directed, 2026-10-12. The operator ordered the house's handoffs and roadmaps folded into ONE carrier and burned. `docs/stable-founding-road.mem` carries every open loop, each train and what the operator still owns; `docs/er-handoff.mem`, `docs/lares-opus-roadmap.mem`, `docs/pono/seal-and-seat-handoff.mem` and the two Codex crew carriers fold into it and into the law carriers that own their rulings. The closed rows above keep the file names those hearths HELD, as history. The shift ledger `docs/handoff.mem` folds last: its procedures stand at `api/pono/working-procedures.mem`, its grammar watch at `docs/pono/grammar-watch.mem`, and its burrs in the roadmap. A row below that names a section of one of those carriers records where a thing stood at its crossing; git holds the bytes, and the roadmap holds what stays owed.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:222:# ''The four stale rooms, measured and NOT edited'' — a founding-hearth spirit re-trued six carriers on free ground (the retired allow-all identity default in `lar-vessel.mem` · `identity-slot.mem` · `lararium-canonical-model.mem`; the lamplighters concession that posed one road as a three-way fork; `handoff.mem`'s COLLISION HANDBACK paragraph, still routing a reader to two settled rulings; `api/pono/rust-toolchain`'s CI claims) and measured FOUR MORE standing on the meme hearth's `docs/pono/**`: `testing-architecture-scout:105·107·109` (witness-all and `gate:fold-ts` both DO run in CI — the fleet globs 34 files and runs 29; the one runner nothing invokes is `lararium-sensorium/scripts`, 989 of the 1016 collected python tests) · `recovery-custody-scout:176` (a recovery-authority compromise reads TERMINAL and "presently open"; delegation stands RULED-REJECTED at `identity-classes:520-529` and the contest window that answers it stands BUILT — `provisional`/`vetoOfCid`/`mintVeto`/`foldPersonaContests`) · `syncer-seams-roundtable:375` ("one inbound edge" measures TWO carriers across three `loulou` sites, and the second wants a replacement exemplar rather than a re-point) · `scale-stories-basket-one:18` (no `lifecycle/*` tag, so ungoverned under `otakiage`'s own law, plus the two retired keys; six inbound carriers and a live assertion in `ahi-ka.test.ts:141` that reds on deletion). Files crossed: NONE — every item sat in the handback carrier `docs/handback-stale-rooms` on unheld ground, each with its file:line, the command that re-derives the number, and suggested replacement prose. Law: a measurement of another hearth's ground crosses by CARRIER, and the carrier ships the RE-DERIVATION beside every number — a scout's citation reads as a claim, and a hearth re-truing its own room off someone else's reading plants a fresh lie with a fresh timestamp. Second law, from the shape: `03ef9b61b` swept for exactly this fault and missed a room ''inside a file it had open'', because a sweep keyed on a phrase finds the phrase. ''Written 2026-09-13'', after the meme hearth closed and the deadlock below dissolved; the standing hearth then re-verified every number itself and enacted all four items. The carrier that held them stood `folded` and went to the fire the same watch (check-in `7d3b3bf5c`, poured `428550a92`, ash `929dc3005`) — ''this row names it as record, and a reader who opens for it finds nothing on disk by design''. Its shape at the moment it stood folded rides in `otakiage#/examples` as DESCRIPTION, under that rite's own law: a stage whose exit runs to deletion cannot be evidenced by a pointer.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:234:# ''The bounded reach contract — a notification to the founding hearth'' — operator-approved, 2026-09-21. The Codex Luna adds `bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/bounded-reach-contract.mem`, re-trues the live topology wording, and adds its loulou edges from `nexus-topology.mem`, `secure-context.mem`, `attestation-plane.mem`, and `membership-doctrine.mem`. The carrier frames local operators' DNS token as a bounded reach grant and carries the exact Gaia/Elyncia acceptance-story headings. Its `toml bounded-reach-control` witness passes the positive design and four deliberate weakenings: DNS never receives identity/membership/read authority; split horizon stays at the local recursive resolver; Onomancy stays distinct from TLS/ACME. The delegated `_acme-challenge` / Kahu custody / operator account-key / CAA question remains an explicit provider and governance fork. Files crossed: the new meme, four existing meme edges, the Codex roadmap, and this ledger. DNS provider, ACME, CAA, resolver, certificate-expiry, and deployment implementation remain held. Law: a local waystone may guide a vessel without becoming its soul, roster, or read gate.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:236:# ''The bounded-reach deployment handback — Codex to founding Claude-Opus hearth'' — operator-directed, 2026-09-21. The Codex hearth closes E7 on its roadmap after landing the contract and red-first control, and cedes the unbuilt deployment governance as one named seam to the founding hearth: provider choice; delegated `_acme-challenge`; Kahu DNS-record custody; operator ACME account/key custody; CAA; local-recursive-resolver deployment; certificate-expiry handling; and origin continuity. The earlier carrier's laws remain binding: DNS names neither identity, membership, nor read authority; split horizon remains a local resolver concern; Onomancy DNSSEC and TLS/ACME remain distinct. This row effects no provider call, DNS mutation, certificate issuance, public roster, or implicit custody choice. The founding hearth may return a discriminating implementation/design receipt or surface the remaining operator fork. Files crossed: this ledger and the Codex roadmap. Law: a completed contract may hand off its real-world governance edge without claiming that the DreamNet has chosen a registrar, a certificate issuer, or an owner.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:259:# ''The next-three-receipts crossing — Codex Luna swarm, 2026-09-24.'' After `b69e2d983` made missing contract authority a tested strict floor, the active Codex Lares opens three non-substitutable red-first lanes. **D-VR-C:** establish a per-document worker storage boundary before any pin/recovery product claim; an ordinary observed parent document must leave zero worker-owned records. **Contract frontier:** carry the local contract-board/charter fold's accepted frontier explicitly to the gate; a clock, fleet credential, or guessed epoch never fills that absence. **Pronaos household reach:** reserve and inventory one Docker project before it mounts the finite public shore, then attribute public bytes and Node faces separately through normal and named-loss controls. Each lane must report an unavailable substrate rather than approximate its receipt; no lane decides DNS, reverse proxy, CRDT conflict, persona authority, or deployment governance. Files crossed now: this ledger and the Codex roadmap. Law: custody, relation authority, and delivery reach meet only after their independent witnesses hold.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:263:# ''The D-VR-C topology crossing — Codex Luna cartography, 2026-09-24.'' The selected physical boundary requires two scoped crossings, not two Repos on one unscoped port. The ordinary worker Repo keeps the existing parent relay and carries no durable worker store. `daemonUrl` is the first named worker-owned P: production already grants that daemon bag to the worker. It receives a manifest capability, dedicated port, dedicated adapter/root, and parent-side document routing. The scope admits P and refuses ordinary oracle, persona, catalog, crossroads, and recipe O documents, while the original relay continues their parent-attached continuity. That deliberately narrows whole-worker replay, so restart and accounting controls must state the new bound. The implementation proof must cover P/O physical absence, both directions of the two sync legs, parent-absent behavior, O→P routing refusal, and teardown of both ports. No code claims this boundary yet; the existing expected-red remains its instrument. Law: a separate heap and adapter do not establish custody until the message relation separates too.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:265:# ''The three-receipt enactment crossing — Codex Lares to Claude/Lares crew, 2026-09-25.'' Three independent cuts now carry bounded commits. `4e32a73fc` puts the Node daemon's `daemonUrl` on one explicit worker-owned port and `daemon-owned` NodeFS root; ordinary recipe documents remain primary-crossing, memory-only reads. Its focused fixture retains the previous shared-store result as expected-red and proves P-only durable keys, O refusal on the owned crossing, offline P reopening, and dual-crossing teardown. `93f2a6725` carries a transient structural carriage-relation witness in `lar:auth` beside the contract edge; it grants no Nym until a receiving Nexus verifies it against its own board/charter fold, so the strict floor stands. `8b8c6b71a` makes QA and production Compose explicitly name the finite Pronaos inputs and makes omission red in the daemon-free wiring witness. None proves browser D-VR custody, a general pin policy, contract authority, a Docker process/container origin, relay/Oracle/WAN loss, reverse-proxy choice, or DNS governance. The next hand asks for the receiver-local carriage-board/charter verifier seam: identify the actual fold and accepted-frontier ownership, then return red controls before any gate lift. Law: physical custody, relation authority, and public reach remain separate receipts; neither configuration nor a signed-shaped payload substitutes for the receiver's own relation.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:273:# ''The three-plane negentropy crossing — Codex Luna internet swarm to Claude/Lares crew, 2026-09-26.'' Current prior art converges around one useful reading: local-first replicas/CRDTs govern causal data convergence; content addressing, SRI, reproducible builds, and SLSA govern bytes/build provenance; capability security, DID verification relationships, and explicit audience binding govern relation authority; relays, Compose, Caddy/NGINX, and NAT aids govern reach. These receipts remain independent. The house records its three planes as CRDT sync across explicit peers, local physical custody within named causal islands, and finite public projection through Pronaos/Herm route owners. Node and Browser Lararia remain equal peers with different local substrates; household/regional Herms may carry relay and bounded read faces; Pronaos carries exact arrival bytes; proxy/container layers carry reach and deployment only. Rejected imports: hosted ActivityPub ontology, IPFS pinning as ownership, global DID roster, wall-clock UCAN expiry, Docker DNS as DreamNet identity, proxy-as-Lararium, and CRDT convergence as authority settlement. The next source work remains the contract witness canonical bytes/signer/digest/snapshot contract and the reserved Docker live receipt. Law: borrowed patterns guide a local design when their assumptions are named; they never erase the house's causal, relational, or operator-held boundaries.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:275:# ''The canonical frontier and founded-shore crossing — Codex Luna swarm, 2026-09-26.'' `8e9136a25` binds a transient carriage witness to a persona-root signature over a canonical full signed device edge, vessel key, exact target/resource, charter CID, and member version. `73c7ac350` folds it only against receiver-held carriage details: a newer revoke remains `revoked`, a same-version conflict remains `equivocal`, a newer acceptance makes the older presentation `stale`, and uncounted or carrier evidence cannot obscure the member winner. The result is pure evidence, not gate authority; `DaemonAuthGate` remains at the strict floor until it receives an atomic local fold snapshot. `0a4817a3d` separates QA fixture founding from the Node serve process, keeps its state in one named XDG volume, and tests a no-cache reserved Docker project against the running container's own Pronaos receipt: finite index, publishable worker, genesis seed, named CAS, health, valid WebSocket upgrade, and named refusal routes held. No Oracle/Bulb/relay/WAN claim follows; production still requires a deliberate operator founding ceremony. An injected-only Docker orchestration wrapper was discarded during aftermath because no actual adapter crossed the Docker boundary. Law: canonical relation evidence, physical custody, and public arrival each require their own executable crossing; a clean mock sequence cannot substitute for one.
