/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:57:* ''Island doors'': `tools/capability-inventory-witness.sh` measures which vessel doors (fetch · rest · custody write · dyad) each island of the node and web assemblies reaches on the built tree, and every source call that spawns an island or attaches it a door, against the committed table `tools/capability-inventory.json`. The table measures reach, never a door's policy (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/harbor#/the-harnesses">>). A door a class reaches where the table says it did not, a new or extra seam, a seam that left or a new ask reads red by name; a deliberate change re-writes the table in the commit that makes it (`node tools/capability-inventory.mjs --write`). A browser wiki or session island reaches no door and meets the dyad refusal; the browser's daemon island reads `unmeasured`, since its spawn seam stands inside `openBrowserVessel`; a session island's view asks run through the pool core's own listener, which no row drives.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:66:# ''A founding wants a human route on a TTY.'' With no TTY it refuses `CredentialTtyRefusal`, and no flag or environment variable carries a credential. A harness founds through the test door: `tools/test-scratch-marker.mjs` stages the root, `tools/seed-test-custody.mjs` names the published test route, then `lares vessel found --skip-build`; `tools/unlock-test-custody.mjs` opens a marked scratch root. An agent may read vessel state and hand the operator the next founding command as text; the operator performs each founding and custody act.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:80:* ''No global now'' and ''the fence'': #/rulings.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:85:* ''Early alpha'': no back-compat, no shims, no legacy recovery; a stale thing aligns to the current frame and grammar, and a third human's arrival ends that line (#/rulings, the fence) (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/wild-bytes">>). Derive, never enumerate. One function, one relation.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:93:<<~ ahu #/rulings>>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:98:* ''The live test runs with TWO operators on two machines from its first day'': the operator and the operator's daughter, in one house. The face-switch act, the cabal plane, the custody seal and the engine fold ALL land before it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:105:* ''All CODE runs dockerized''; the host keeps only the hooks into the operator's environment (files and bags, session capture, the editor and CLI entry, custody).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:107:* ''A SESSION wears the face; the vessel wears none'' (operator-ruled; quote license: //"a human might want a tab open as one Persona, and a tab open as another Persona... same vessel. Identity as relation."// and //"a CLI session wears its own face too … those act as ephemeral UX"//). A vessel holds its roots and one store. A session — a browser tab, a CLI run — contracts in as ONE persona, and several sessions may live at once over one vessel, each wearing its own. Every act carries exactly one face. Two faces live from one vessel never link on the wire: each session proves itself under its own face-scoped key, never under a key the vessel shares across them. The vessel-wide parts (custody, the daemon island) serve every session and let none read another's planes.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:109:* ''The boundary'' (settled by the house under those rulings): one multi-arch image; `/workspace` mounts bags and wikis, `/state` mounts vessel homes and custody, never an image layer; the local socket stays INSIDE the container and the host CLI enters through `docker compose exec`; the app never receives the docker socket; mDNS offers unauthoritative LAN candidates and a pinned admission alone grants authority; DNS-01 wildcard TLS supplies browser secure contexts; a release manifest binds the image digest to the genesis, engine and grammar CIDs.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:144:* ''The floor key keeps the vessel's public name''; the sealed custody root derives the veil and the sovereign caps. The veil change stays destroy-class.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:146:* ''Locality law'': an unattended ember answers on the local link only, and only where the hearth holds a hardware freshness anchor the ember checks on each ask (#/rulings, the ember's key at rest); a relay pin wants an attending hand. The vessel rests at the floor and raises when t embers answer; the raise lapses by non-renewal, which reads as the raise's next causal boundary (#/rulings, how a raise lapses).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:177:* ''Every boot rests at the floor until a human unlocks'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor">>). At the floor every fleet lane stays shut, and the custody write door, the rest door and the dyad door answer the daemon island alone. A bounded ember stays design input: it raises to SERVING alone, never signs or admits, runs on a count and never a clock, needs the device's own unlock plus a second signal, records each raise, and any other device of the human removes it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:179:!!! The models, each in its own carrier (operator rulings, approved as presented)
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:183:* ''The backup bundle'': a bundle holds ONE face, sealed under a route the person holds, and carries that face's root with its own lines and no key of any seat. Its memory rides as content keys, sealed inside the key island: a bundle opens every surviving value ever sealed under a version it carries, values written after its cut included, and no version minted later. A restore runs as a recovery act that takes a fresh veil and a new seat, and one face on a new device reads as the same audience for the versions that face already held (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:187:* ''Sealed-row acts ride the custody door'', never a store verb whose output lands in the daemon's document in the clear (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:188:* ''Gate keys come in three tiers'': a floor route's keys derive from the floor key, and a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (operator ruling); the serving route's bundle derives from SK, a third tier that leaves those two untouched (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate). A faceless place takes a fourth arm at the gate, the place arm, and a session opens before its certificate. The floor key rests outside the vessel key, and the face proof names what a holder of the disk without the passphrase reaches and never reaches (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:191:!!! Operator rulings, 2026-10-16 ~ approved as the controller's story leans
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:196:* DreamDOM's ruled questions stand in <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom">> #/open-rulings.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:198:!!! Operator rulings, 2026-10-18
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:199:* ''Each browser tab asks for its own unlock.'' A tab that attaches to the shared holder opens the keystore by its own ask of the person; the holder carries no unlock between tabs. The reason reads off the session law: a session wears its own face, so each tab answers for its own opening (#/rulings, a session wears the face). The ask admits a tab to its face's open hive and derives no key: the holder keeps a face's keys while some session of that face stands unlocked, and the last to close locks it (operator, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">> #/what-both-faces-hold). Row `B1` carries the build.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:201:* ''On the node, the boot marks the unlock and the session marks the face'' (operator, 2026-10-18, approving the house reading). The per-tab ask binds browser tabs; a node unlocks once per boot through its custody door, and every CLI run, MCP seat and watcher proves its own face at the gate without asking again (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">> #/the-node-scope).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:203:* ''One Keyhive identity per PersonaGroup, none above them'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18: //"it's the only way to retain control over faces that don't know about each other"//). Each face's PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, its event store, its registry, its archive and its content-key seat; no vessel-wide identity registers a face's bags, delegates them, or holds a face's group. Two faces of one vessel then never link on the wire, a removal from one face rolls that face's bags alone, and a bundle restores one face and nothing of another. Today the vessel's own identity registers every bag and delegates each face's bags through itself, and the vessel and every face share one event store and one content-key holder (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/keyhive-per-persona-group-2026">>). House readings under the operator's confidence, each naming what flips it: a herm keeps a floor-only transport key, behind a red test that it can neither author, resolve nor observe a face's capabilities, and holds no Keyhive identity if that test fails; several face hives share one process only after a substrate probe reads them isolated, and each face's hive runs in its own worker otherwise; co-mingled history migrates by fresh identities and an old mixed archive refuses by name, with no bridge; a founder that cannot leave its group leaves by a fresh PersonaGroup. Row `K15` carries the build, folding `W25` and `K12`; `W26`'s slice 3 waits on its face context.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:204:* ''A cabal shares through the faces its members choose'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18, on the Teshima Family Council story). Kalani founds a private family council; Leilani, already standing on the DreamNet with several faces, chooses which of them join it, and a face she keeps back never learns the council exists. The council's hive reads as a Keyhive group with no key of its own: its members act through their own faces' identities, so nothing stands above them, and a presentation reads valid against the current set without naming which member made it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/identity-classes">> #/the-handle-chain). Any current member's face promotes into the council's canon; a graft takes the threshold; a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` at the threshold or a fork that omits the captor (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">> #/the-unswept-corner); members read the owner-set as faces, never as humans. A private council declares no heraldry and lives in its members' address books under pet-names (cabal-realm #/heraldry). Row `K16` carries the story as `K15`'s acceptance.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:205:* ''The asker seals'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19, F6's custody fork). Once the browser holder owns the Repo and the daemon kernel, it routes each sealed write to the admitted tab whose session caused it, else to any admitted, unlocked tab of that write's face; with no awake admitted tab, the write waits, named `seal-awaits-session`, never silent and never decided by a clock. No key material leaves a tab, and each sealer holds the row-class key the occupied carrier's overwrite proof opens. A SharedWorker carries no promise to run while its tabs freeze, and no `MessagePort` event reports a peer's death (round one, 2026-10-19), so a seal that waits names its wait.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:206:* ''A face's custody rows seal under its own key'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19). Each PersonaGroup holds an independent random face custody key (FCK) that only its own slot tree opens (passphrase, paper or PRF), never wrapped under the vessel key, so a holder of the S key or of another face's unlock opens none of its rows. Face-private rows: each face's veil archive, face-key custody, guardian sets, face-provisional, the fleet-join address secret and record, a pending join bound to its target face, the per-face device shares, and each face's partition of the handle book and roster; the vessel Keyhive archive splits per PersonaGroup under `K15`. A face bundle carries that face's identity, archive, FCK recovery route and guardian set, and nothing of a sibling. Today every hot and cold custody row seals under one S key (`vault-carriers.ts`, `browser-custody.ts`), so face isolation reads as routing alone until this lands. Row `K15` carries the build, and `F6` slice three lands with its step 3. How a vessel-common act unlocks dissolves (next ruling).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:207:* ''A shared act never makes a shared secret'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19; four ratcheted research rounds, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026">>). Every act that touches more than one face sorts one of three ways: its private bytes DISSOLVE into the owning face's rows (D), its public bytes stand at the FLOOR by design (F), or it names a vessel SECRET (S) whose principal and opener the house names row by row. A mixed carrier splits before it sorts. The browser holds no vessel key: founding, fleet join, slot changes, roster, archives, handle book, dyads, restore and clear sort D or F, so each tab asks only its own face's unlock and public floor work asks nothing. Phones, installed web apps, probes, the CLI, MCP and watcher seats and a native shell hold no S. A tablet waking floor carries ciphertext and public rows unattended and decrypts no face's row. A container restarts at its floor and nothing unlocks it unattended. A guest island that owns a key store stands as its own vessel. A node holds S only for rows it names: the serving key has no row yet, so it guards nothing today. * ''The place signs by a scoped signer under a pre-rotated KEL'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19; a fifth research round, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026">> #/the-place-signer). A node's place identity keeps a KEL whose inception commits the next key, and that next key rides the founding card beside the seed charter's cold next key, offline; the online place signer runs unattended for an enumerated allowlist of floor duties alone (the KEL's own events excepted, which the card's key signs), rests under the host's TPM-bound credential where the host offers one and an owner-only file elsewhere, and never rides an environment, an image or a log. A stolen online signer rotates away by the card; a lost card beside a stolen signer re-founds. The floor holds no custody key; it holds its own named place signer. The format change rides the founding bake (`X0`). The place KEL commits its next cold key on the founding card and rotates by that card (`W29`), and the seed census names every reach of the seed past the floor, K15's owed bonds among them (`tools/seed-census.mjs`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:208:* ''Custody and identity read by capability, never by host'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19: //"I consider node and browser isomorphic-by-intent. Eventually, a browser-vessel somewhere may grow comparable capabilities to a node vessel, and this pattern cascades outwards to all future vessels."//). Three rules hold on every vessel, present and planned: a vessel meets each face through that face's atom alone, its veil signing every dial, join, enrolment, sibling channel and daemon proof made on that face's behalf, never one device-wide key; a vessel holds a place signer exactly while it stands a floor, for the floor's allowlisted duties, under the pre-rotated place KEL; and a faceless vessel reading another's floor proves nothing private, reading the public shelf under the floor card's pin. A node's daemon auth, device-key signer, sibling enrolment and group-secret opener read the one vessel seed today (`open-node-vessel.ts`), and a browser's do the same (`open-browser-vessel.ts`); each is a bond owed, carried by `K15`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:209:* ''Identity enacts a bond'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19). Lineage stays within a root, and covenant joins roots: a root (a compartment seed, a vessel key, a face custody key, a charter seat, a content key) derives children for its own duties alone, and any identity spanning two roots is a bond, an act both ends sign that seats a fresh key of its own, resting with the end whose privacy it serves and lapsing by its own act; no closure holds a root (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/identity-enacts-relation">> #/identity-as-bond, its seven laws and bond table).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:216:!!! House rulings under the operator's delegation ~ the questions the operator delegated, each with what flips it
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:218:* ''The ember's key at rest'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A separate serving key (SK), the fifth custody class `serving`, wrapped by the vessel key and by ember slots, seals the serving rows alone, and the serving tier holds no minting secret: a walker's grant checks under a public half, a shape the hosted road's re-cut lands before the ember's walker arm. An unattended answer (any slot that answers without a person's confirm on the ember) needs a freshness anchor a disk copy cannot carry, a hardware-sealed hearth key whose attestation the ember checks on each ask; without one every ember slot answers only on a person's confirm, threshold two buys a second confirm and never an unattended raise, and after any counted removal a bare deny-only `sk-rotation-owed` mark refuses every ask until SK rolls, a mark a rolled-back disk copy can omit. ''For the operator'': a hearth that holds no hardware anchor raises only on a person's confirm. The reason: a key that opens serving state opens nothing beside it, and a copied disk replays any freshness it carries; the ruling flips on a threat review showing the serving rows hold nothing a thief can use even before the grant re-cut (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:220:* ''How a raise lapses'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A raise lives one boot and lapses at the next causal boundary (a lock, a restart, a human unlock, a counted removal), and that boundary IS the expiry the waking floor requires; no timer and no heartbeat ends a standing, and the count spends at the raise ledger's durable commit before SERVING composes, so a crash before the commit spends nothing and serves nothing and a crash after it burns the raise. The reason: quiet never tells a slow device from a gone one; the residue: a rolled-back ledger on a disk copy restores spent raises. The ruling flips on a causal renewal event every reader receives that also survives the ember's loss (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:222:* ''The outbox at rest'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Each outbox parcel seals under randomized authenticated encryption with a stable outbox key the vessel key wraps and an unlock hands the daemon island, the way content keys reach it, and rests under a random name with its routing inside the sealed body, so a locked disk names no reader; the `sealed-outbox` row leaves `floor-plain` for a sealed class. Before a parcel's atomic commit nothing stands sendable, after it the parcel re-opens and retries at the next unlock, and after a ship and before the local delete the receiver folds a repeat idempotently. The reason: a reader digest on a stolen disk names a relationship; no flip stands expected, since the ruling closes a residue (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:225:* ''The restore's key history'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A restored face stands PROVISIONAL until at least one party to its relation (a sibling device of the same human, a seated chair of its Nexus, or a guardian) shows its own log view and that view agrees with the restore's head; while provisional the face reads, recovers and serves its own content and signs no authority-changing act, the restore prints which head it read and from where, and the provisional state names who could confirm it. Where every such party stays unreachable, the guardians' recovery path (the impersonation quorum) answers, never the local read alone. The reason: no vessel reads a head it never received, and the house keeps no registry of heads; no flip stands, and the residue stays stated: one agreeing party may itself sit stale (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:230:* ''Engine cadence'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Cadence keeps its own lineage and threshold, apart from every seat key. A Nexus's joint founding cites one cadence inception that names each founder's hearth, the device that bears the reboot, as a holder; a household seed carries none, since its one holder bears its reboots. Each hearth mints its cadence key at random on the device, never derived from serving or floor material, and keeps it, with its next-key commitment, as a `cold` row under the vessel key that unwraps per act; no sixth custody class and no extra card at the founding. A holder may later rotate onto a cold card by its own choice. Each island pins one engine epoch, and one daemon hosts two epochs only as two separately pinned islands. The reason: the people who bear a reboot decide it, and a seat-holder who runs no hardware forces no one's restart. The ruling flips on a cadence act that must run unattended where a per-act unwrap cannot (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:232:* ''A restore after guardian enrolment'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). A face's own bundle restores after it enrols guardians, so long as the face's log still holds the set its own root enrolled by the typed first event and no later event moved it; a guardian rotation that moves the set cuts every earlier bundle off. The restored face stands provisional as the restore's key-history ruling holds. The reason: enrolling guardians must never silently kill a person's own backups, and the guardians' rotation, not the enrolment, cuts off a stolen bundle. The ruling flips on a provisional gate that cannot stop a restored face from signing an authority-changing act before a party confirms it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:233:* ''Paper restores a root, never memory'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). The split-root cards rebuild the persona root alone; content keys stay random and wrap under the vessel key or a bundle's own key, and no key the root derives opens memory. A person recovers memory through a bundle, under the route that bundle seals. The reason: a root card that opened memory would turn every share holder and every thief of the paper into a reader of the face's private bytes. The ruling flips on an explicit choice that root-share holders read memory, with the custody that choice costs stated.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:236:* ''The working address'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). A face's working document takes its id from a dedicated face address secret: 32 random bytes minted once per face, sealed on each of that face's vessels, delivered to a joining vessel by the fleet-join door, and moved only by a deliberate rotation act that opens a fresh working document; neither a per-Nexus key's re-issue nor a vessel key touches it. The id reads as the first 16 bytes of HMAC-SHA-256 keyed by that secret over the length-prefixed domain tag `lar/working-address/v1`, the wiki relation's stable id (the face's `wikiId`, never a recipe CID, a composition fingerprint or a label, so a recipe edit or a rename moves nothing), and the slot kind in its lowercase spelling (`draft`, `working` or `personal`; `temp` holds no document). Each working document starts empty, with no initial change, so two offline vessels of one face converge on one history; a vessel's first write lands as an ordinary change. The reason: two devices of one face open one notebook offline and sync into one, while a keyed id lets no observer link two faces or read the secret. The ruling flips on a face identity contract from train N that already names shared face-secret bytes with the same custody and rotation.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:248:* ''The channel of intent'' (operator, 2026-10-20: //"Approve your leans, land the full models into the architecture now"//). The daemon wiki keeps working memory; a face's intents travel on that face's own intent plane, `@intents-<tag>`, a fifth face plane beside the four; a vessel's own records rest in its daemon bag, unmirrored; the face's pins rest in the face's custody and `@persona`. The approved leans: the plane stands from the first landing, never staged in the daemon bag; the winner reads by the intent's own preference list, else the lowest `H(atom ‖ intent id)`, and never elects; a single-effect fleet-wide verb never addresses "any device", and a human answer may name its executor; a claim never expires, a device's staleness stays a local suspicion, and the operator's release always wins; an `every` intent reaches a later-joined device unless its bound names a roster edge; a far agent reaches the plane through a relay seat, opt-in per face and ring-gated, its research before its build; an intent voids by supersession, a revoked delegation, a passed roster edge or the operator's cancel; compaction folds by the operator's act, never a timer; a local verb that touches its own vessel alone bypasses the plane and leaves its receipt in that vessel's bag. The plane carries a hand's decisions that cross devices, never its motion (the rubric, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">> #/the-rubric). Row `I1`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:251:* ''Sync carries; verification decides'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the research at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/identity-invariants-2026">> and the controller's leans). A mutable CRDT carries identity claims and never decides them. Each face holds, on each device, a ''sealed identity anchor'' in its own custody (a D row): its PersonaGroup, its persona-KEL prefix, a commitment to its root, its device edge's digest, and a known frontier that never falls. Only founding, admission and the recovery rites (guardian rotation, bundle restore, root cards) write an anchor; sync never writes one. Founding and admission acts, device edges and lease advances travel as signed records in the face's `@persona` plane, a signed-entry log every reader verifies against the anchor and the KEL; two signed acts at one sequence surface as a fork, never a CRDT winner. The face planes hold verified projections. A device reads freely; an act that widens authority (admit, grant, re-key, seal to a reader) checks the sealed frontier and refuses a target that names a newer bound, its receipt naming the frontier it acted under. Transparency and witnesses for equivocation wait for their own row. Wave C carries the build inside `K15` step 6.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:252:* ''Wave B's forks'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's leans). A fresh PersonaGroup mints a fresh atom, never an orphan's seed. A tab reads its face's pins from its custody anchor before it opens its session, so the tab's own Repo retires; and each face holds its own social planes in the browser, keyed by PersonaGroup as on the node. Both ride Wave C with the anchor.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:254:* ''The order of the next waves'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's leans). Wave C (`K15` step 6 under the identity anchor) runs next, with `W26`'s slices 3, 4 and 6 beside it on the floor's own ground, their composer hunks passing to the controller as patches, and slice 5 after it, since its accepted floor rests as a face's sealed row (a D row under the face's own FCK once Wave C lands); `I1` follows the anchor; the far agent's relay seat takes its own research after `I1`; `G37`'s renames ride `X0`'s bake; the sensorium resumes after `X0`, on the operator's word.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:281:* ''The socket's handshake changes once.'' R-WIRE and the face proof build as ONE wire train: the signed admit, then the fleet-join door, then one socket cutover (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof">>). The tree between those steps reads no earlier shape; it stands as a build order, never a compatibility mode.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:305:(#/rulings) bounds the whole road: every slice that changes a shape lands before the second operator seats a key in the first Nexus.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:310:and the six paths disagree, operator-ruled order governs: the engine fold and the custody
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:314:* ''The receipt ledger's direct leg'': the three receipts of #/rulings stand where a CLI meets its vessel (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger">>). The leg across a herm rides THE WIRE (`W12` of #/the-loops).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:316:* ''Retired bags, the evergreen sweep and custody's edges'', itemized in #/the-loops (`G5` through `G7`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:330:* ''What stands sealed'': the custody root and the `identity-anchors` family: the keyhive archive, each face's own veil archive (`veil-archive-g<group digest>.bin` on the node, keyed by its PersonaGroup; the browser's `veil-archive-h<N>` row still keys by handle index until `K15` step 6), each face's anchors and the anchor roster. A founding seals them from its first write and hands out every keyhive Archive it stood before the provider leaves; the veil derives from the sealed custody root; a seat (`custody-seat.ts`) carries one holder per identity home, and each row reads whole or refuses by name, never empty. A creator that stands again restores from its Archive: cap events carry membership and never a creator's key agreement state. A stand mints one contact card and its Archive leaves after that mint, so the Archive lineage opens every prekey the identity ever presented. A browser vessel keeps the Archives its founding and its admit hand out in its keystore beside the device seed, in the clear, until browser custody wraps both (`browser-keyhive-archive.ts`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:331:* ''Every writer family rests under its custody key'': the carrier table (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>; `vault-carriers.ts`) names `floor` and `floor-plain` outside the vessel's keys, `hot` and `cold` under the vessel key, `serving` under SK, and `outbox` under an outbox key the vessel key wraps. SK mints at the founding; a human unlock opens it through the vessel key's entry in its serving tree (`sk-slots`, a bare `floor` row; `serving-key.ts`, `custody-session.ts`). Serving rows and ember slots stay owed (`E2`); sealed outbox parcels stand, while ship and delete stay owed (`K13`). Each sealed row passes through the one sealed writer (sidecar → re-open → compare → rename, never sealing in place) and the sealed open. The per-face backup bundle stands built, cut and restore.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:332:* ''No keyring stands'' (operator ruling, #/rulings): the code holds no per-Nexus convergence secret. No custody row, seat mint, admission delivery or charter commitment carries one, and a persona admission's signed transcript names no keyring digest. A private body seals under its bag's content key, which reaches its readers through a lockbox (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/keys">>). A seat's act and a roll mint nothing beside the charter epoch. The same ruling's standing law binds every later slice: let a counter, wherever one appears, order one writer's own emissions only; keep the face at the session capability; keep every verified fork head visible; retain by causal evidence.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:333:* ''The handle-book'': the recogniser's handle-book rests sealed under the S key. Nothing at its path reads as a book that recognises nobody; a row that stands and does not open, or opens to another shape, refuses by name at every read and every write, and a save lands only over nothing or over a snapshot that reads whole (`packages/lararium-node/src/node-circle-store.ts`). The follow graph holds one home, the persona-scoped circles plane the daemon's circle verbs write, and no custody row carries an edge.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:335:* ''The vessel-identity family'': the persona roster, the worn-face selector, the pet-name map, the declaration map and the published-face record rest sealed under the S key as hot rows; each persona root rests as a cold row, opened for one act; the floor vessel key rests beside its signed inception, every load proves that inception, and no next-key seed or commitment rides it. The roster commits a root: a mint writes the root row, then the roster line that carries the root's public key, so a reading of a public key answers off the hot roster and opens no root. A root row with no roster line reads as an orphan: no reader holds it, `lares persona list` names it, and the same mint run again adopts it. A roster line whose root row went missing, or names another key, refuses by name at the act that needs the seed, and nothing mints over it. A hot row with nothing at its path reads as holding nothing; a row that stands and does not open, or opens to another shape, refuses by name at every read and every write. A vessel key mints only inside a held custody, and lands with its inception under the custody's one claim: the key file commits the mint, so two acts never commit two keys, and a boot loads a key and never mints one. The floor reads no row of the family, so a carried-Nexus reading by persona (a seated chair, a kept consent) answers empty until the key arrives, and a sovereign composition reads the roster whole before it stands (`packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`). A floor composition reads no roster, so it shuts every fleet lane: it sorts every device as set aside, sets a proven sibling aside, and its fetch door reads no peer as fleet, the pinned join gate's key included (`packages/lararium-node/src/floor-fleet-lanes.ts`). It still folds the one fleet board its own device edge names in the clear, so the Binding Gate reads this vessel's own seat at every standing.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:337:* ''The walk records'': each hearth a vessel walks at keeps one HOT row sealed under the S key, named by a digest of that hearth's gate key (`packages/lararium-node/src/node-walk-store.ts`). A record holds bearer invites, the hearth's grant and one receipt per carried document (`{ cid: "blake3:<hex>", ref, key }`, whose `key` opens that document), so it counts as a secret row. The row rests in the storage home of the custody seat: the store takes no directory, so no caller files it beside a document store the vessel key never spans. Nothing at a hearth's path reads as no walk there; a row that stands and does not open, opens to another shape, or rests filed under another hearth's name refuses the read, the list and the update by name, and an update seals a whole record or nothing. Each change reads, decides and seals under one custody holder, so one invite leaves a wallet once. A floor composition reads no walk record and presents no walk; a fresh browser device stands at the floor under its `#floor=` card, and a joined face crosses under its root-signed pin. A key that locks under a live walk costs the walk one message, which it logs. `lares walk`, `walk take` and `walk invite` ride the custody door (`walk.state` · `walk.take` · `walk.invite`): a carried invite as a verb's argument, or an invite as a verb's outcome, would rest in the daemon's document in the clear.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:338:* ''The hosting rows'': a hearth's hosting state, each spend and its walkers' carriage rest as HOT rows sealed under the S key, in the storage home of the custody seat (`packages/lararium-node/src/hosting-store.ts`, `hosting-carry.ts`). The sealed writer writes a whole file and appends to none, so each spend lands as ONE row of its own, named by a digest of its nonce or marker: the row's presence IS the burn, and it reads, decides and seals under one custody holder. The spend row commits a redemption, and what rides ahead of it re-derives: the grant from the epoch, the leaf, the nonce and the claim, so a crash before the answer replays as `retry`; the operator's counts from the rows standing, by name. A roll's state row commits the roll, and the hosting doc re-derives from it: the next roll and each sovereign stand land an act the sealed state holds and the doc lacks (`landHostingActs`). The sweep of dead epochs' rows passes through the seat's removal door (`removeCustodyRow`), which removes only a row this vessel's key opens; a spend that sealed after a roll retired its epoch burns nothing live and leaves with the next sweep. Each carried value rests as one row whose name carries its address and its length, so a guest's bytes read off its rows and no counter stands beside them. One process serves a hearth's carriage (the standing vessel's own gate, under its store claim), and its contacts and deposits run in turn, so a quota reads the bytes the last deposit left and a reclaim never discards on a reading a contact moved meanwhile. A row that stands and does not open refuses by name: a burn nobody can read never reads as unspent, and a carried value nobody can open never reads as absent. A floor composition reads no hosting row, so a locked hearth sorts no socket as a walker. `lares host`, `host roll` and `host invite` ride the custody door (`host.state` · `host.roll` · `host.invite`): a minted invite as a verb's outcome would rest in the daemon's document in the clear.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:339:* ''The seal ceremony'': the growth rite's two rows rest HOT under the S key in the seal home (`packages/lararium-node/src/seal-ceremony.ts`): `transition-pending.json` prepares a crossing, and `transitions.json` commits its record. A seal verifies the crossing whole, appends its record (the commit point), then removes the pending row, only while that row still holds the crossing it sealed; a seal that committed and stopped resumes to one kept record and no pending row, and kept records with no pending row read clean. A chair's own seat key signs for the ceremony behind the custody door (`seat-key-store.ts`), and only what the standing state licenses: `seal.sign` names a seat by its public key and signs a charter roll that steps from the standing head, reveals at least that head's count of the seats it committed one digest each, seats only keys this vessel holds and re-arms every seat it seats, where the charter's lineage verifies and its head binds the seated roster; it refuses every other image however well formed, and a persona root holds no seat row, so it signs no roll; the rite's hands mark through `crossing.open` · `bind` · `sign` · `witness` · `seal`, which take no image and sign the crossing that stands open (a face's seat keys sign; a witness's root attests). The rite arms itself behind the same door (`seat.arm-genesis`, `seat.arm-roll`): each standing chair's seat key mints there, each chair's NEXT key prints once as a cold-key card the operator reads back before the charter moves (a staged test root alone stands in), a roll adopts each card's key as its chair's seat key, and a superseded seat key retires once no held charter seats it and no open crossing names it (`seat.retire`). An earlier charter shape reads by name (`nexusCharterShape`) and licenses nothing. ''No command file writes a custody row'': a census derives every sealed row's name, every write door and every writer function from the carrier table and the custody modules, and reads red on a command source that calls a door, names a writer function, or names a row beside a file-system write of its own (`packages/lares-cli/tests/custody-write-census.test.ts`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:340:* ''The face proof's rows'': `face-proof-key` rests COLD, one face's proof key at one Nexus, held by the root-holding vessel alone, its file named for the face so that face's backup bundle carries it; `vessel-face-key` rests HOT, this vessel's own face-scoped key, and stays on its vessel, outside every bundle. Fleet join calls the certificate and grant path; the removal and gate session paths still need the socket cutover. Two doors on the custody seat sign and return (`signAsFace`, `signAsVesselFace`): each signs exactly the image handed in under the key its scope names and hands out no secret, and a store never lands over another standing key (`packages/lararium-node/src/face-key-custody.ts`; the library names the shapes in `FACE_PROOF_CUSTODY_ROWS`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:341:* ''The gate's two root doors'' (specified in code; no composer calls them until the socket cutover): a floor gate's bundle derives through the floor key's door, which answers at a locked vessel, hands back a fresh child and never the floor key (`vesselFloorKeyDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`); a sovereign gate's bundle derives through the custody seat's door, which answers only while the seat holds its key (`custodyGateDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-seat.ts`). The doors carry two types, so no line swaps them by accident; a root refuses the other tier's door by name; each seat's door refuses the other tier's child; and a weld holds the two mints to the two seats (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:342:* ''The gate's memory rows'' (specified in code; no gate calls them until the socket cutover): a sovereign gate's withdrawal memory rests one row per face key in the vessel's storage home, named by the face's proof-subject digest and sealed under the S key, so a locked vessel's disk names no face key (`gate-memory` in the carrier table; `packages/lararium-node/src/gate-memory-rows.ts`). Each write reads, decides and seals under one custody holder, and refuses where it would drop an event the row holds; a locked seat refuses by name. An older copy of a row restored by hand makes a gate forget until the next honest vessel dials, and no fence stands against that hand. A row that stands and does not fold whole refuses by name and reports it (`GateMemoryRowTorn`): the asking gate falls silent, no keep writes over the row, and a person repairs it by hand, where a row read as nothing would let a fresh memory admit a vessel the row once denied. No backup bundle carries the row: a vessel that stands again knows nothing (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-withdrawal-proof">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:343:* ''The session and the boot'': the daemon stands at the floor holding no S key and unlocks on a custody frame of its owner-only socket (`unlock` · `lock` · `custody` · `act` · `backup`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-frames.ts`), handled ahead of every verb, so the credential the CLI reads on its TTY reaches no receipt, outcome or log. One holder keeps the opened S key in node-main (`custody-holder.ts`); an unlock tears the standing composition down and stands a fresh one on the same floor (`open-node-vessel.ts`), a lock returns it to the floor, and three failed unlocks spend a boot's attempts. A composition that refuses above the floor leaves the floor standing and names its fault once. The settle sweeps a sidecar whose write never landed. The test door (`tools/unlock-test-custody.mjs`) opens marked scratch roots alone, and the marker earns one loud line in `vault status` and the boot log. Every boot composes at the floor: nothing stored lifts it. A daemon island holds no S key, so its archive exports cross the custody write door (`custody:write`) and the main thread seals them. Every broad sync port, the daemon island's and each wiki island's, crosses one hardened facade on both ends: an arrival that reads as no sync message drops at the port and never reaches a listener that would throw on it (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/island-repo.ts`). The daemon island's gates ask the main thread what a device's edge reads on its fleet's board through the dyad door (`dyad:ask`), which answers `aside` wherever it cannot read. Each fold of the fleet's edge board sets off the key side's settle on an unlocked vessel, with no timer and no person: the main thread places the island's `seat-duties` verb, awaits its answer and keeps the signed rolls (`packages/lararium-node/src/seat-settle.ts`; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/what-the-code-holds">>). Those two doors and the rest door answer the daemon island's channel alone: each worker's class binds at its spawn (`packages/lararium-node/src/worker-handle.ts`), a wiki island reaches the fetch door alone while its custody write and its rest ask refuse by name and its dyad ask draws `aside`, and a session island reaches no vessel door. A command that acts with no vessel standing opens its own key session at the first sealed row it touches (`packages/lares-cli/src/offline-custody.ts`): a terminal prompt, and under a marked scratch root the published test route. A sealed row's act rides an `act` frame of the custody door and never a store verb: one typed table bounds the acts (`packages/lararium-node/src/sealed-acts.ts`), a standing vessel answers with no second prompt, and beside a standing vessel a command opens no key session of its own, while a root's recovery split refuses there (`packages/lares-cli/src/sealed-act-door.ts`). The fleet mirror of a pet-name and a declared Handle rides that door too: `selves.carry` names a face and which name, the vessel's main thread reads the name off its sealed row and writes it onto that face's own persona plane and no other face's, only where that plane's rest seals (a clear rest refuses the carry and the name stays on its row), `lares persona sync` fills and never replaces, and no verb takes or answers a face's own name (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:344:* ''The per-face backup bundle, its cut'': `lares vault backup --face <N> --out <file>` cuts one face's bundle through the standing vessel's custody door, under the law at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-cut">>. The carrier table's bundle column picks the rows, the frame asks the vessel's own route again, the daemon island seals the memory section to the pair the bundle key derives, and the command binds the bundle's routes in its own process (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-bundle.ts`; `packages/lararium-node/src/face-bundle-cut.ts`, `custody-frames.ts`; `packages/lares-cli/src/vault-backup.ts`). The handle-book tags each record with the face that recognised it, so a bundle carries its own face's records alone. A node vessel's daemon island stands its content-key holder off the document it owns; no content key mints on a production vessel until a session signer stands, so a production cut carries an empty memory section.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:345:* ''The per-face backup bundle, its restore'': `lares vault restore <file>` brings a face back onto a fresh vessel as a recovery act, under the law at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>. The vessel checks the root against the newest key history it reads, seals one commit row, lands the carried rows additively, and lights the face through the face rite: a new seat under the same fixed prefix (`packages/lararium-node/src/face-bundle-restore.ts`; the act table's `bundle.restore` and `bundle.import` rows; `packages/lares-cli/src/vault-restore.ts`). The rehearsal runs end to end on scratch roots, on the real doors and on standing vessels of the built tree. `--memory` lands the bundle's content keys through the island's import door; on a production vessel it refuses `signer-unavailable` until the wire cutover opens a session signer.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:346:* ''The custody door and its census'': `lares vault` answers seven verbs (`status` · `unlock` · `lock` · `bind` · `unbind` · `backup` · `restore`), and a credential rides a terminal alone: no flag, environment variable or pipe carries one. `vault status` gives ONE reading of each standing file, derived from the carrier table: a `hot` or `cold` row reads sealed or reads as a fault, a row outside the S key prints the law it rests bare under or reads as a fault where the file breaks that law, and a private file in the three homes that no row names prints by name (`vault-carriers.ts` `outsideTheTable`; `custody-session.ts` `custodyStatus`). `vault unbind --rotate` runs as one act: the rotation's census and its opening of every carrier pass before any byte moves, so a carrier that refuses the rotation leaves the slot bound. `tools/custody-census-witness.sh` founds a vessel on a marked scratch root with the built tree and refuses an owner-only file, a seal or a sidecar outside the table; it carries that rotation to its end on the founded vessel. The law, each bare row's reason and the residue a row's name leaves at rest read at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:352:* ''The harnesses stand on the image'': harnesses run the built image by digest and bind no source tree; the mesh scenarios name their own compose project (`MESH_PROJECT`) and feed their browser vessels from the image; the browser CI runner alone reads the repository read-only. Each harness opens the vessel it staged through the test custody door and reads a hearth as stood only once that door answered an open key; `mesh-scenarios all`, `harbor-walk-witness`, the crossing and herm witnesses, the browser walks and the household HTTPS witness all stand on that shape (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/harbor#/the-harnesses`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:356:Build order: the realm and signer shapes against the rulings; then R-CHARTER, the one train that moves
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:363:''R-CHARTER, the one AID train.'' Its first stage stands landed (train K of #/the-trains): the chairs sign with seat keys of their own and pre-rotate on cold cards, a Nexus answers to `nexus-<sha>`, the floor key founds by a clockless self-signed inception (its next cold key committed since `W29`), per-Nexus keys mint at random, the PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, and the Stable founding act founds a hearth (`lares vessel found --hearth`): the place, persona zero and a PRIVATE seed charter at one seat, with no keyring, every fleet relation bound to that charter's AID, and every harness that founds a hearth founding through it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook#/found">>). What stays owed:
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:365:* ''The cadence inception'' cited once by a joint Nexus founding, never by a household seed: its shape stands in <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract">>, and its holders stand ruled (#/rulings; `K9`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:369:* A per-Nexus wire key in two tiers (operator ruling): a floor route's bundle derives from the floor key and answers at a locked vessel; a sovereign route's bundle derives from the sealed custody root and stands only while the vessel stands unlocked. One gate per (Nexus, route), so knock, pin, verdict and posture read per Nexus exactly (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>). The serving route's third tier rides train E (`E3`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:379:* ''R-KAHU'' stands witnessed: a two-of-two charter whose seats live on two vessels opens, cosigns and lands a cabal admission and a promotion, each vessel under its own scratch root (`nexus-cabal.test.ts`, `nexus-promote.test.ts`). The co-signed `keptBy` fills the realm's steward map (#/rulings).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:412:* ''What blocks rung 3 onward'': rung 3 waits on ONE FACE. Rung 4 waits on HARBOR's household HTTPS, on the KAHU PLANE's grant for a foreign leaf, and on browser custody: a browser leaf holds a passphrase or paper slot before it holds a persona root (#/rulings).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:426:Each row names what stays owed, the train of #/the-trains that closes it, and who owes a ruling first
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:428:the row; a line number drifts, so none rests here. Train letters: ''S'' the custody seal · ''G'' ground ·
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:433:* ''#/stride-1-spine'' — face and custody; sealed identity and private authority.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:437:* ''#/operator-gates'' — operator rulings and hands.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:446:Face and custody ground, then sealed identity and private authority; the face anchor precedes the planes that inherit it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:450:* ''Integrity owed: face isolation, end to end'' (`K15` step 3, `B1`; `F6`'s slice three rides here with Wave B). Its witness: one adversarial multi-tab, multi-face run in a real browser, an unadmitted port, a stale generation, a cross-face sealed write and the last session's lock, where today only fake islands read them. MEASURED (the fresh read of Wave B; the readers, 2026-10-20). Wave B (PR #81) builds the guards and their reds on fake islands and the node; the real-browser adversarial run waits on Wave C's one SharedWorker per house.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:451:* ''Integrity owed: identity authority enforced, beyond the prose'' (`K15` step 6). Its witness: Wave C's red suite, a forged selector and a coherent foreign bundle refused, one sequence signed twice surfacing as a fork, a frontier that never falls. LEAD on the suite's shape; MEASURED that today's gate verifies continuity alone (`boot-daemon-keyhive.ts`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:453:* ''Research pair: the far agent's relay seat'' (`I1`'s relay phase). Its question: the least relay trust and attestation that stops capability escalation and argument substitution while keeping causal provenance. Lenses: protocol security / distributed failure semantics.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:457:* `G7` Custody's edges on train N's ground: a short seat can write a charter that boots torn (`nexus-seal.ts`); a floor-class carrier standing alone founds, which decides whether a new custody adopts a standing vessel key (identity ground); `setFoundingRoute` stands as a test seam in source (`found.ts`). N.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:459:* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the S key included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Lead: DreamNet-Wright after `W26`'s floor slice lands. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) landed in PR #88. Wave D (the FCK fence, its eight slices whole, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) landed in PR #95 on 2026-10-26: each face seals its D rows under its own FCK, unlocks apart, bundles and restores alone, lifts its anon veil on join, and seats when its grant arrives. `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:460:* `B1` Browser custody. The custody API stands specified in `browser-custody.ts`: a passphrase or paper (2-of-3) slot binds the slot tree, the device seed and every Keyhive Archive move into sealed carriers through the mesh's one sealed writer, a wrong route refuses and changes no byte, a locked keystore refuses `sealed-locked` before any mint, and the clear-password act asks through the confirm door and answers only to a literal yes. The boot stands (PRs #48 and #61): the vessel lock gives back on a throw and a `sealed-locked` boot retries in the same page, the web boot asks the unlock through its own form, the clear verb answers `asks` and calls no door before a literal yes, the wiki's `tm-clear-password` road asks through TW5's confirm road and writes no synced tiddler, the question names what it clears, and a declined unlock retries in the page. Under #/rulings (a shared act never makes a shared secret) the browser holds no vessel key, so the clear names one face and clears that face's rows, built inside `K15` steps 0 through 3. Owed: the persona roots, which still rest in the clear outside the tree, sealed under it, with the mint refusing until a slot binds (#/rulings); the browser's vessel-key rotation; and the passkey slot, after its derivation gets measured (`B3`) and never alone. Each tab asks for its own unlock, and the ask admits that tab to its face's open hive while the holder keeps a face's keys only while some session of that face stands unlocked (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; the research and its leads at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">>). Built with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder answers a port only for a session it admitted, an unadmitted port asking for a sealed body refusing by name, and the last session of a face to close locks that face's hive; the production holder lifecycle stays a named skip on every engine until Wave C's one SharedWorker per house. B.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:461:* `W4` The face-scoped proof chain: face key, the vessel's face key, the session key. The subjects, private authority, the session signer and the session face supplier stand specified in code, and the withdrawal proof reads as a house model the operator may overturn (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-withdrawal-proof">>). The two custody rows stand in node (`face-key-custody.ts`); fleet join calls the certificate and grant path, and `openJoinedFaceSession` stands. Owed: the browser holder of the face's custody rows. House. W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:467:* `F11` The hands: the watcher as a leasing session, the seat under a standing grant, the Mask as a record field, door parity at the session (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands">>). An agent's dissent drafts and a person's direct ask edits (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). O1.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:468:* `K12` A fresh PersonaGroup for a seat no hand can revoke (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/keys">>). The PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, so every other seat's revocation rolls the bags the group reaches (`persona-group-roll`); revoke authority follows the seating lineage, so a seat whose seating hand left, and the founder's own seat, leave only by a fresh group. Owed first: a name the face keeps across groups, since its plane names key on the group's id. It builds inside `K15`'s per-face removal step. K.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:472:* `G34` A removal no reader can keep refuses by name (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/automerge-doc-store">>). The store lands a based removal a concurrent writer overrode, then surfaces it to a listening reader alone: with no parallel-drafts reader it drops the surfacing with no word, and a reader that throws earns one console line while the write stands (`automerge-doc-store.ts`, `parallel-drafts.ts`). Owed: the refusal by name before any change lands, wherever no reader stands or every reader failed, with the store authoring no draft of its own; and the durable conflict handle the refusal carries (the document, the removal's request id, the conflicting change and head identities, never the hand's text), at a home where a hand whose editor went offline finds it again. G.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:473:* `G35` The disk watcher's standing instruction (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/projection-law">>). Owed: the instruction as a record the operator signs by a human route, naming one bag, a path pattern and a per-wave count ceiling, which no automated seat signs; the watcher's settle of each pending removal it covers through the shore's removal door; the audit row that names the instruction a removal rode; `lares shore restore` over a settled removal; and a mass vanish past the ceiling, a standoff, or a removal outside the pattern left pending for a person (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/watch.ts`, `shore-verb.ts`, `disk-projector.ts`). G.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:482:* `K16` The Teshima Family Council (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>), `K15`'s acceptance story. Kalani founds a private council; Leilani joins it with two of her three faces. Red-first, after `K15`'s face context: (1) the council's hive as a Keyhive group holding no key of its own, its members the chosen faces' own identities; (2) an invite walks Leilani to the door, the threshold grafts each chosen face, a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` or a fork by omission; (3) a member face's photo lands in its working layer of the council wiki and reaches the council's canon by `MOVE` (`W27`); (4) both chosen faces read it, the face kept back reads nothing and learns nothing, and no event in the council's history names a creator or issuer that ties two of Leilani's faces together; (5) a herm carries the sealed book and authors nothing (`K15` step 5). The e2e set stands four vessels: Kalani's, one per chosen face of Leilani's, and a herm. The e2e set walks the council at one hearth first: Kalani's seed charter holds the realm and Leilani's chosen faces walk there as guests, no Nexus founded (#/rulings, one charter). The two-hearth council follows, under the Nexus the two found, and there the member consult that lets a realm's documents cross between two operators reads a root map nothing fills (cabal-realm #/many-realms, owed), and the climb from seed charter to Nexus re-pins the realm by a named act (owed). Open joints: a quorum Handle with a seated key stands only where the council signs as one name, and that key signs collective acts alone, reaching no member's hive (#/the-steward-signer, owed). K, W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:484:* `P9` The re-seal proof and the fork-resolve act stand ruled (#/rulings): the re-seal record builds with sealed-store step three, the fork-resolve act in train N.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:486:* `I2` The far agent's relay seat (`I1`'s relay phase, handed on at `I1`'s land, 2026-10-26): the least relay trust and attestation that stops capability escalation and argument substitution while keeping causal provenance. Its research pair stands above (''Research pair: the far agent's relay seat''); its build follows that research, before founding. I.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:488:* `W12` The herm route for cancel and the three receipts, as ruled (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger#/the-relay-leg">>); no code asks, cancels or answers across a herm. Owed, with `W9`: the ask, the cancel and the vessel's answer as a tagged inner frame under the sealed sibling session's own seal, the vessel reading that session's proof as the asker's; the herm's bare delivery note inside the session, bound to the ask's unique request id and the session's causal position, attesting transit and never execution; and the rule for which verbs a sibling's standing reaches across the session (`sibling-channel.ts`, `uds-channel.ts`). W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:489:* `E2` The serving key's custody and its unattended road (#/rulings, the ember's key at rest; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>). Built: the fifth class `serving` in the carrier table, read by the census and `vault status`; SK minted at the founding; `sk-slots` with the vessel key's entry, opened at every human unlock and re-wrapped by a vessel-key rotation. Owed: the serving rows under SK and SK's own rotation; no minting secret in any serving row; the anchor path, where an ember slot answers unattended only against a hardware-sealed hearth key whose attestation the ember checks on each ask; the confirm path, where every slot of a hearth with no such anchor answers only on a person's confirm and threshold two asks a second confirm, never an unattended raise; and the bare deny-only `sk-rotation-owed` mark that any counted removal sets and that refuses every ask until SK rolls (`vault-carriers.ts`, `keyslot.ts`, `custody-seat.ts`). E.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:490:* `E3` The serving gate's tier (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>). Owed: a third tier name in the route type, its bundle derived from SK under its own registered domain, its pin, and a pin's move by a signed causal event or a verified key-history step alone, with no quiet period that ages a pin out (`gate-bundle.ts`). E.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:491:* `E4` The raise's commit point and its lapse (#/rulings, how a raise lapses; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>). Owed: the count spent at the raise ledger's durable commit, before SERVING composes, so a crash before the commit spends nothing and serves nothing and a crash after it burns the raise; and the raise's lapse at a lock, a restart, a human unlock or a counted removal, with no timer and no heartbeat that ends it (`custody-seat.ts`, the raise ledger's writer). E.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:493:* `H8` The grant's signed shape and public-half verifier stand specified in `walker-grant.ts` (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember#/the-tiers">>). Owed: the live roll that derives grant public halves for serving rows inside H's one act cut, before E's walker arm. H.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:511:* `W26` The system wikis release and every other wiki reads the floor (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Slice 1 stands (PR #49): genesis carries the first floor, its manifest and the `lares` and `lararium` snapshots by CID, and `@oracle` reads that floor by CID. Slice 2 stands (PR #52): each vessel's system, crossroads and realm pointers rest in its own `@catalog`, and nothing writes the shared `@oracle` after genesis (`oracle-doc-no-writer.test.ts`). Slice 3 stands (lane `--w26-floor-3`): the founding lands the counted 1-of-1 Kahu admission for persona zero's group (`landFoundingAdmission`) and registers `lares` and `lararium` as realm bags of the hearth's realm under persona zero's per-Nexus key (`landKahuRealm`); `kahuCabalCanonAccess` has its production caller (`kahuReachSourceOf`); the keel mounts only what the realm names, the registered bag set and the `bags/` mirrors follow, and no catalog row names a system bag. Slice 6 stands: one predicate (`requireKahuReach`) guards the residency reactor, meme put and delete, draft placement and a realm steward's write, and the keyholder island's verifier carries it for `--in-wiki` verbs. Slice 4 stands: the release (`floor-release`: body, CID, steward seal by a seated Kahu key, the cabal's high-impact approval of the manifest's exact bytes, the charter's epoch lineage), the chain fold, `lares nexus release`, the porch (`GET /floor/<Nexus AID>`, `/cas/<cid>` for the head's blobs), the browser's verified read, and the flow map's own `flow-pointer` domain in place of the retired `oracle-pointer`. The build runs six slices in order, under the architecture of #/rulings (2026-10-18), its shape and evidence at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane">>: (1) the floor manifest and its read-face, genesis baking the first floor; (2) each vessel's pointers leave the shared document for its bootstrap, re-cutting `W21`; (3) the Kahu realm holds the live system documents, and a one-seat founding lands its 1-of-1 Kahu admission; (4) the release answer on the crossroads, folding `P8`; (5) the accept act per (face, Nexus), which follows Wave C's face context since its accepted floor rests as a face's D row; (6) reach into system canon refuses every hand outside the cabal. OWED: a browser Kahu hand rides Wave C's face context (the browser composes no board reader and reads as a stranger, fail closed); a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until that context carries the charter and the board to it; the carriage `canon` names (`device-admit.ts` `admitCanonDocs`, the browser's `hearth-canon`) read rows nothing writes now, and retire with `W21`'s rest. W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:520:* `W29` The place signs by a scoped signer under a pre-rotated KEL (#/rulings, the place signs by a scoped signer, 2026-10-19; kit <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane">>): built, PR #98, 2026-10-26. One KEL grammar (`vessel-kel.ts`, beside `persona-kel` and `handle-kel`): the inception seats the online signer and commits a cold next-key digest; a rotation reveals that key, which signs it, seats a replacement signer and commits a fresh next key; no interaction events. Every founding door, node, hearth, herm kindle and browser alike, mints the armed inception and lands no byte before the founding card reads back through the `PlaceFoundingCard` port, and the cold seed rests on no file. `lares vessel rotate` runs the card ceremony: it verifies the old card against the head, reads the replacement card back, then stages, publishes and reconciles under one custody claim, and a restart never invents a successor. Peers learn the head from the Nexus carriage board and an offline herm from the carry bundle; one fold, bounded at 64 rows and 8 pieces of fork evidence per AID, refuses a gap, a rollback and a fork. The five floor duties sign and verify `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage`. A seed census names every raw-seed consumer and fails on a new one. Owed: a browser ceremony UI that seats a card (until it lands, the browser's KEL door refuses by name and a browser leaf holds no place KEL); the seed's other reach, K15's bonds, named in the census. Since `W14`–`W16` (PR #100), the floor pin duty and the carrier seal resolve their signer at the head (`verifyPlaceDutyAtHead`, `verifyCarrierContractAtHead`), and a flow pointer reads its publisher off the verified head. W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:532:* ''Integrity owed: the bake's cross-product'' (`X0`, touching `K15` step 6, `W26`, `G37`). Its witness: one matrix over the pre-bake and post-bake artifacts, every old CID refused after the bake and a fresh two-of-two founding standing, rather than greens read row by row.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:538:* `G37` The evergreen sweep of 2026-10-18 (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/evergreen-sweep-2026">>, its six rulings and fourteen lanes). Built: (1) the standing witness `tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` (PR #53), its ceilings version 59 (F6's envelope took five), clock 57 (the engine watch took two, the cap-event rows one) and narration 202 (W27 took one) over 1079 files; (8) the engine watch reads an engine by its sha256 (PR #60); (5) worldline replay orders by parent links and handle dependencies and names every skip (PR #62), the mempalace KG still dropping `parentKey` when it persists and the CLI tree's sequential mark still reading recorded times, each exception naming its rule, file, line, count and reason; (2) `bytesEqual`, `constantTimeBytesEqual`, a strict `hexToBytes` and `nexusAidOfPin` in `@lararium/mesh` (PR #51). Order of the rest: (3) opaque ids, the mount nonce, optional display times and parent-link worldline replay, after `W26` slice 2, the clock sinks at effect-record, residency-actions, sense-sensorium, handler-args, engine-watch, wiki-behavior, verb-tiddler and vessel-mailbox; (4) the engine watch by CID, the `LarDoc` and session-envelope shapes, the floor announcement's kind and the browser store's current shape; (5) the numbered preimages and formats renamed together in the bake that closes `W26`, the signing preimages outside `domains.ts` among them (holder-continuity, persistence-keel, wax-stamp's `lar-*/v1`), which take the same frozen-preimage ruling as `engine/v1`. Each lane red-first under a clock set to 1970 and to 3000. G.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:539:* `X0` The founding bake: one deliberate re-genesis before a second operator stands, after which CIDs are meant to last because another operator pins them. It moves together `K15` step 6 (identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, archive and custody formats, each face's random device veil), the place KEL's pre-rotation and the scoped place signer (the signer frames each duty's domain itself, signing `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` and its verifiers the same, so no signed floor image carries its own separation; built with `W29`, whose readiness red reads a fresh genesis founded armed, the five framed pairs verifying, and an old-shape inception refused by name, `old-shape-inception`), `W26`'s closing bake (the floor release), and `G37`'s preimage and format renames (`engine/v1` and its kin, the floor announcement's kind, the genesis seed and CAS formats). Each member carries its own readiness red, so the bake waits on the slowest by name, never on a date; the bake's own red: a fresh genesis founds, no CID from before the bake verifies after it, and a mixed old archive refuses by name. The gate it opens: a second operator may found a Nexus fresh at two of two. X.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:570:* `K13` The sealed outbox (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>). Parcels rest sealed under random names in the `outbox` class. Owed: carriage shipping, idempotent receipt and local delete after ship. K.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:571:* `K14` The restored face's provisional standing (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>). The mark, guardian or chair view, confirm verbs and three authority-changing refusals stand. Owed: provisional guards at the root-signed crossing, edge kapae, device admit, two-founder act and session signer's authority purpose; a sibling view needs independent proof; the guardians' recovery path where every party stays unreachable. K, W, N.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:574:* `P8` One public answer per Nexus, signed by the steward: the floor release answer, built as `W26`'s release slice (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): the body, the steward's seal, the approval and the porch stand (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu">> #/floor-release). The domain's Handle table stays here, off the ceremony's chain by ruling. P, W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:575:* `P17` The realm feed's writer check: the feed verb runs in the daemon island (`cabal-realm-verbs.ts`), while the worn face's key at a realm's Nexus mints on the vessel's main thread behind the custody door (`cabal-face.ts`), so the verb resolving its own writer needs a door from the island to the vessel, the shape of `dyad:ask`, which moves the capability inventory and the compose files. The one production caller, `lares cabal feed`, names that key through `cabal-face`; the residue: a caller that types any writer. P.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:578:* `W10` The knock tests offline for a reader holding candidate pins and the clear path (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`, `knockSegment`, `gateKnock`): CLOSED as a named leak by the operator's ruling (2026-10-26), the sovereign route's promise leaving a pin-holding path reader outside it (face-proof #/named-leaks; the reading at `docs/pono/w28-gate-lane` #/the-knock-reading). More research owed later: whether a secret selector, its first-dial bootstrap and its causal re-key on every removal earn their cost, read again when a sovereign pin escapes its members' custody, when route confidentiality against pin-holders enters the promise, or when hearths commonly stand many Nexuses behind one address; a flip after `X0` moves the dial's URL bytes by its own versioned rite. W, canon.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:582:* `W20` Burned names outside the wire's files still guarded by name. The porch burned every such guard outside `K15`'s held files (PR #102, kit `docs/pono/porch-lane`): the browser's burned-store absence check, and the retired verbs, flags and exports in the CLI, vault, nexus and cabal tests. The CLI's unknown-command refusal reads generic, with a nonsense control. What remains rests in `ceremony-core.ts`, `keyhive-provider.ts` and `boot-daemon-keyhive.ts`, and burns with `K15`'s bonds lane. W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:588:* `F6` The browser holder as owner, with unicast replies. Slice one stands (PR #56): a closed routing table (`holder-routes.ts`) sends each island message to exactly one port, a reply by its request id, camera traffic by its lease, the island's own asks to its owner port, and drops a kind with no route by name. Slice two stands (PR #58): every tab-to-holder message rides a random owner epoch, a session and a generation, and the holder refuses a stale or unknown one by name to that port alone; `session:open` with its face waits on `W4`'s face supplier. Slices three and four move the Repo and the daemon kernel into the holder; their sealed writes go to the asker (#/rulings, the asker seals). Slice three stands with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder routes each sealed write to the session that caused it, and Chromium, which exposes no nested Worker inside a SharedWorker, takes the dedicated-worker floor, its swap waiting for the worker's `ready` before it replays the manifest and retiring the crossing it replaces. Slice four stays owed. O1.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:590:* `F9` The switch; the vessel-wide selector retires. Its one persisted shape, the selector's two stores (the node's active-persona index and the browser's `ACTIVE_PERSONA_STORE`), retired with `K15` Wave D (PR #95): the worn face lives as session state on node and browser, and no store keeps it. The switch act itself lands additive. O1.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:634:* Guardian count and threshold remain with the operator (#/open); bundles carry enrolled guardian sets and the restore checks them (#/rulings).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:655:* `E1` The ember: the serving tier under its own key, the ember pin, the raise with its count and record, four roads of removal (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember">>). Its three questions stand ruled (#/rulings), and `E2` to `E4` carry what each ruling owes. E.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:658:* `W21` A joinee mounts the hearth's `@lararium` corpus read-only beside its own, while the oracle plane never crosses (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Each vessel's pointers rest in its own `@catalog` (PR #52), so a joined vessel's pointer no longer replaces its hearth's, and `shared-oracle-doc.probe` holds that two synced vessels each keep their own. The rest rides `W26`'s floor slices: a joinee reads its hearth's floor by the release and its CIDs (slice 4), where slice 5's accept act moves its pin; a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until Wave C's face context carries the charter and the board to it, and `device-admit.ts` states the law. W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:659:* `W25` The carried bag event names its creator in the clear, where the WHO plane's veil-born group hides it: measured red (`packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/bag-event-creator.probe.test.ts`, lane `--w26-own-canon`); `K15`'s step 2 hides it, since no vessel-wide identity then creates a face's bag (#/rulings, 2026-10-16 and 2026-10-18). W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:660:* `W27` A write reaches its wiki's working layer (#/rulings, 2026-10-18). Built (PR #55): `LOAD` into a canon bag refuses, naming the promotion it owes, while genesis and founding seed through their own named door; an act aimed at a bag opens the bag's own wiki, its recipe record or the floor, through one mesh record-or-floor export the surface recipe and the node's open and act paths share, and lands in its working slot; a mount that cannot stand refuses by its cause; the daemon wiki keeps the daemon's own reach. `W24` walks it. W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:662:* `K17` The edge frontier (#/rulings, the edge frontier, 2026-10-20). Red-first: the frontier certificate and its verifier on node and browser alike; the signed empty genesis at every founding; registration of a raise into its signer's next frontier; the widening reader (admit, grant, a content-key seal) acting as of a qualifying frontier and waiting as unknown otherwise; the admit bundle carrying the frontier and its snapshot; the reader persisting its highest accepted head. Reds: a withheld first raise, a deleted local raise, a stale clean frontier, two conflicting frontiers, a missing snapshot, a concurrent raise and lower, an epoch rollover. Beside Wave C, on the spine. K. The fleet board's frontier stands built with Wave C. The realm leg, K17-R (kit `docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`, the operator's rulings on forks 3 and 4, 2026-10-22), landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26: one lease law, so a Nexus or realm lease rises only on a charter quorum's signed advance read under its seal-epoch lineage and the unsigned max-register retires with no reader left; each voucher signs its own hand's frontier; a seal roll signs every anchored realm's head under the new epoch; a split-seat cosign carries its head; and the realm admit bundle carries the board's acts, frontiers and snapshots, so a joiner holding no board acts as of them. The closed roster's window passes to `K18`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:663:* `I1` The face intent plane (#/rulings, the channel of intent, 2026-10-20; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">>). Build order, each step red-first: `@intents-<tag>` minted by the PersonaGroup with its entry kinds (intent, outcome, asks and answer, claim, release and takeover, supersede and cancel), each signed by its device's atom and its id a content hash; stand-down and the three verb classes, with a single-effect verb addressed to "any device" refused at issue; the read-side winner; causal voids and the operator's release; the face-join summons moving off the daemon doc onto the plane, which closes two hearths of one face, beside the CLI naming its face per invocation; the daemon wiki's view pane; the rubric's witness (a hundred keystrokes and a save write no entry; one move writes one intent and one outcome); then the far agent's relay seat after its own research. Its reds stand at the carrier's #/the-reds. Its authority reads stand on the face's sealed identity anchor, so it builds after Wave C lands the anchor (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's lean); the relay seat's own research wave follows it. Lead: a Sonnet Episkopos with a Sol and a Copilot seat. I. Built, PR #99, 2026-10-26 (kit `docs/pono/i1-intent-lane`): `@intents-<tag>` stands as the fifth face plane, registered by a signed `plane` act and never projected to disk; each entry signs under its own domain over the signed-act image, the intent id hashing issuer, verb, arguments and nonce; a device stands down on an answered slot, a single-effect verb addressed to a class or "any device" refuses at issue and an unpinned one waits on an `asks` gate whose `answer` names the atom; the winner reads by preference, then the lowest `H(atom ‖ intent id)`, with every duplicate kept visible; claims, takeover and causal voids read no clock, a finite `every` names a roster act on `@persona` and waits while its reader lacks it, and the persona root, the face's operator key, signs the release that outranks a claim; the face-join summons rides the face's plane (`lares intent issue|show|ask|answer|claim|takeover|release|cancel|supersede --face N`), the daemon-doc verb retired, and the effect door fences the pinned hearth and the operation id before any re-key, so a second hearth refuses and a replay returns its grant; the daemon wiki shows intents through a read-only pane; the rubric witness reads a seeded duplicate before trusting its zero. The far agent's relay seat passes to `I2`.
