/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom.mem:17:role              = "dreamdom — the house's full DreamDOM model, evergreen. DreamDOM names the WHOLE concept: the superset of cameras over one headless TiddlyWiki engine, every HTML5-capable device and every surface the research waves targeted (the browser on the Node vessel's box, other browsers and WebView shells, the Node-served browser and SSR face, QuickJS and Hermes shells, the UE6 sidecar, Mudlet, MCP and chat, the canvas), each a (root template, document sink) with its two-way capability named per surface. Carries the four layers and two waists, the camera reading, the width dial, the Wiki Actor and the first surface, the position (four unusual, three borrowed), the fork and its ruling (keyed absolute frames, the grain declared at mount), the three crossings up and the UP-leg contract, what a sink beside the engine must keep, the three layers of a TW5 surface, the confirm road, the five un-skipped sites, conformance (filter-cts, camera goldens, interaction goldens), the seven pono vectors, the moʻolelo draft, the open rulings and the testimony. The older sense, the two-instance replacement for `$tw.fakeDocument`, reads as one member: the browser DOM sink at width none. Collide against `dreamdom-prior-art`; walk the build by `dreamdom-roadmap`."
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom.mem:30:''The older sense reads as one member.'' This carrier once pet-named the house's replacement for `$tw.fakeDocument`: a document instanced twice, one in the wiki VM and one on the main thread, with the thread boundary inside it. That member still stands, hardened: ''the browser DOM sink at width none'' (#/the-width-dial), with its keyed absolute frames down and its answered events up. Its rulings carry to every member, since every member faces the same two legs.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom.mem:34:''What this carrier carries as ruled, and what as read.'' Operator rulings of 2026-10-11 and 2026-10-16 stand marked where they fall. The rest reads as the house's design: a contract with parts unbuilt, each part named as such in `dreamdom-roadmap`. The moʻolelo (#/moolelo) stands as DRAFT, awaiting the operator's blessing.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom.mem:183:''Two surfaces on one actor.'' Two tabs at width none each open their own surface under their own session; the actor mounts one camera per surface. `$:/state`, popups and the confirm question live in the engine today, so two surfaces see one popup state (the confirm road rules this acceptable for one question; the open ruling on `$:/state` per surface stands at #/open-rulings). Two tabs at full or skinny hold two replicas under one leader (a Web Lock elects, a channel announces, a late tab gets a snapshot and never a `ready` it missed). Two devices merge in the CRDT; a peer write into an open editor reaches the page as a descriptor and the page keeps the person's text with a //take theirs// affordance beside it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom.mem:343:`lar:service{requestId, kind: clipboard · download · route · open-surface · print · fullscreen · open-external · http-request, args, userActivation: true}` travels engine → surface; the surface answers `service-result`. A surface's manifest at `session:surface-open` lists the kinds it carries; a kind outside the list answers `page-action-unavailable` at once and the engine raises `$:/temp/lares/alert/refused/<kind>`. Of the fifty-odd `tm-*` kinds the core dispatches, the navigator's, the fieldmangler's, `tm-confirm`, `tm-edit-text-operation` and `tm-verse-event` run in the engine wherever it sits; the twenty that bind only under `platforms: ["browser"]` split in half: pure wiki logic the island registers itself in a startup module (`tm-rename-tiddler`, `tm-relink-tiddler`, `tm-home`, `tm-modal`, `tm-show-switcher`, `tm-notify`, `tm-scroll` and `tm-focus-selector` as hints) and host services each surface names or refuses. `tm-http-request` opens a gated door under a person's act (#/open-rulings), never an ambient fetch.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom.mem:402:''The reading of this direction into build'' now stands in `page-controls`: the first three page-native controls as ruled (a field editor, a popover, a disclosure), the designed set, the naming convention (a template names a vessel-shipped, allowlisted custom element in light DOM and never supplies script), the wire, the refusal words, and the shadow-widget verdict per stock widget. Still owed: which stock surfaces refuse meanwhile, pinned by the interaction goldens (#/conformance), and the open ruling on the browser DOM sink's edit template (#/open-rulings).
