/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/swarm-harvest/the-selective-disclosure-address-book-findin-588208.mem:115:8. **Cross-app identifiers reconstitute themselves server-side within a year.** Kollnig et al., FAccT 2022 (N=1,759 iOS apps, before/after ATT): ATT works as designed — only **24.7%** of post-ATT apps can reach the IDFA, and **60–95%** of users refuse — *"but the number of tracking libraries has – on average – roughly stayed the same"* (3.7 → 3.6; **86.39%** still carry one), and pre-interaction tracking domains rose 4.0 → 4.7. The measured reconstitution: *"we found **9 apps** that were able to generate a mutual user identifier that can be used for cross-app tracking, **through the use of server-side code**"* — Umeng's "AAID," an Alibaba subsidiary, **violating Apple's policies**. General mechanism, stated plainly: *"large tracking companies can likely still use these identifiers to build profiles… using their server-side code to link different identifiers together (e.g. through the user's IP address, other device information, and first-party data)."* Their PETS 2022 companion (N=24,000 apps): AdId shared by **55.4% of Android / 31.0% of iOS** apps; device model + phone name by **85.1% / 61.4%**.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/realm-bag-brief.mem:46:# ''One doc id both sides name.'' Two vessels that each mint their own `bags/lares` doc hold two docs under one name; the live system documents now rest in the Kahu realm, registered once at the founding (`packages/lararium-node/src/kahu-realm.ts`). A relation-carried bag needs a doc whose id DERIVES from the relation, the way a face's planes derive from the PersonaGroup doc id (`personaScopedBagIds(personaGroup.docIdHex)`, `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/ceremony-core.ts:329`): `realmScopedBagId(realmDocIdHex, slug)` — a pure function of the realm's own name, so both stewards compute the same address from the charter they both hold and find it with no registry consulted.
