57:* ''Island doors'': `tools/capability-inventory-witness.sh` measures which vessel doors (fetch · rest · custody write · dyad) each island of the node and web assemblies reaches on the built tree, and every source call that spawns an island or attaches it a door, against the committed table `tools/capability-inventory.json`. The table measures reach, never a door's policy (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/harbor#/the-harnesses">>). A door a class reaches where the table says it did not, a new or extra seam, a seam that left or a new ask reads red by name; a deliberate change re-writes the table in the commit that makes it (`node tools/capability-inventory.mjs --write`). A browser wiki or session island reaches no door and meets the dyad refusal; the browser's daemon island reads `unmeasured`, since its spawn seam stands inside `openBrowserVessel`; a session island's view asks run through the pool core's own listener, which no row drives.
59:* ''Known environmental reds'': `lararium-tw5` `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts` (Chromium legs) and `tests/meme-routes.e2e.test.ts` fail where no browser or server socket stands; the browser suite reads `no tests` under a `HOME` that holds no Playwright Chromium.
66:# ''A founding wants a human route on a TTY.'' With no TTY it refuses `CredentialTtyRefusal`, and no flag or environment variable carries a credential. A harness founds through the test door: `tools/test-scratch-marker.mjs` stages the root, `tools/seed-test-custody.mjs` names the published test route, then `lares vessel found --skip-build`; `tools/unlock-test-custody.mjs` opens a marked scratch root. An agent may read vessel state and hand the operator the next founding command as text; the operator performs each founding and custody act.
80:* ''No global now'' and ''the fence'': #/rulings.
85:* ''Early alpha'': no back-compat, no shims, no legacy recovery; a stale thing aligns to the current frame and grammar, and a third human's arrival ends that line (#/rulings, the fence) (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/wild-bytes">>). Derive, never enumerate. One function, one relation.
